{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000147153789": {
      "title": "Technical Officer - Simulation and Practical Experience (SPE)",
      "description": "Looking to step away from shift work, while still using your healthcare skills? Join Griffith University as a Technical Officer - Simulation (Nursing and Midwifery) to support the delivery of realistic learning experiences for Nursing and Midwifery students. This hands-on role involves preparing, maintain and supporting clinical teaching laboratories and simulations spaces ensuring equipment, facilities and consumables are ready for student learning. Perfect for someone who enjoys the practical side of healthcare, this is a technical support role rather than a teaching or clinical care position. No night shifts, no weekends. Weekday hours, with shifts between 7am and 6pm, and a positive work-life balance. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Prepare and maintain clinical teaching laboratories and simulation environments for Nursing and Midwifery students. Provide technical support for practical classes and simulation-based learning activities. Manage equipment, consumables, stock control and procurement to ensure resources are safe, available and fit for purpose. Promote safe and compliant work practices, supporting Work Health and Safety requirements across learning spaces. Work collaboratively with academic and professional staff to deliver high-quality student learning experiences and continuous improvement initiatives. About you What matters most is your commitment to making a positive impact. You’ll bring practical, reliable and service-focused approach, with experience in healthcare, clinical learning or technical support environments. You take pride in creating safe, well-prepared learning spaces and enjoy hands-on work. With strong organisational skills, attention to detail and a proactive mindset, you can manage competing priorities while delivering high-quality outcomes. You will also have: Relevant health qualification, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Experience providing clinical, laboratory, simulation or technical support, ideally in healthcare, tertiary education or clinical skills environments. Demonstrated ability to maintain safe, compliant learning environments, with strong knowledge of Work Health and Safety practices. Strong organisational, communication and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders. Practical experience supporting clinical learning spaces, simulation environments, equipment and resources, with proficiency in Microsoft 365 and a willingness to learn new technologies. Experience supporting Nursing, Midwifery or other Health discipline simulation activities is highly regarded. A current driver’s licence is desirable. What we can offer \nThis is a continuing, full-time position primarily based at the Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 4 range $76,126 - $80,321per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $89,067 - $93,976 per annum. \n\n Why join Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Anna Marshall, Team Leader - Clinical Skills and Simulation at anna.marshall@griffith.edu.au. For application and recruitment advice, please Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at m.mahon@griffith.edu.au Closing date:  Wednesday 16th September at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000147146579": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Clinical Psychology and Internship Coordinator)",
      "description": "As a   Lecturer (Clinical Psychology and Internship Coordinator) , you will use your skills and experience to advance clinical psychology training and professional practice education and drive meaningful change. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Lead high quality clinical education through engaging, student centred learning and assessment across postgraduate psychology programs. Coordinate and strengthen all Psychology Clinic placements, ensuring seamless operations, clear communication, and exceptional professional standards. Build excellence in clinical supervision by providing individual, paired, and group supervision that supports safe, ethical, evidence based practice. Collaborate with Clinic and Program leadership to shape future focused training models, assessment processes, and placement pathways. Contribute to key academic activities, including OSCE delivery, postgraduate selection, and advisory committees to uphold program quality and compliance. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at Griffith University Nathan campus. As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. \n\n What matters most is your drive to create a brighter future that benefits all. Through our core principles of excellence, ethics and engagement, you’ll thrive on seeing the direct and lasting impact you’ll have on every community and every future. You will also have: A postgraduate qualification in psychology, registration as a psychologist in Australia, and clinical psychology area‑of‑practice endorsement. Eligibility to provide supervision under Psychology Board of Australia requirements. Demonstrated experience supporting postgraduate learning in clinical or professional psychology settings, with the ability to guide students through complex practice‑based challenges. Strong organisational capability, with the judgement and professionalism required to manage sensitive information, competing priorities, and dynamic clinical training environments. Excellent communication and relationship‑building skills, enabling effective collaboration with academic leaders, clinic staff, students, and external partners. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Allison Waters, Head of School - School of Applied Psychology at a.waters@griffith.edu.au . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at m.mahon@griffith.edu.au . Closing date:  Thursday, 17 September at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The School of Applied Psychology are a leading education provider offering accredited degrees in psychology, counselling, suicidology and health services management. Our programs emphasise practical skill-based learning and the application of disciple knowledge across diverse professional settings. Graduates are equipped to support individuals facing personal, health, vocational or social challenges and to lead impactful initiatives within the health sector.",
      "department": "School of Applied Psychology"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000147098729": {
      "title": "Integrity & Complaints Officer",
      "description": "About the Opportunity  The Integrity and Complaints Officer provides expert advice and guidance to investigators and specialist teams on procedural integrity across complaints and integrity-related processes. The role supports the timely, consistent, and compliant resolution of complex matters, while contributing to the development and implementation of strategies, solutions, and business process improvements that enhance the management of complaints and associated processes. Key responsibilities Provide frontline advice and intake services for complaints and integrity matters, assessing enquiries and referring issues to appropriate channels. Receive, assess and triage complaints, academic integrity matters, reviews and appeals, conducting initial risk assessments and referrals in line with University policies and legislative requirements. Manage low-risk student matters, including providing advice and supporting early resolution where appropriate. Coordinate complaint administration throughout the case lifecycle, maintaining accurate, confidential records and ensuring compliance with information management requirements. Provide administrative and secretariat support for complaints governance activities, including the University Appeals Committee. Support the annual Declaration of Interests process through system administration, enquiry management, monitoring and reporting. Maintain and improve complaints and integrity frameworks, processes, systems and resources to support efficient and compliant case management. Monitor trends, risks and systemic issues, providing insights and recommendations to support continuous improvement. Develop and maintain complaints and integrity guidance, content and training resources. Foster collaborative relationships across the University to support effective case management and promote a culture of integrity. About you Completion of a relevant tertiary qualification or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. What we can offer \nThis is a full time, continuing opportunity primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 6 – Base range - $94,966.18 - $101,295.51 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $111,110.42 - $118,515.72. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Thursday 17th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "General Counsel"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146886199": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant",
      "description": "Griffith Health Clinics provide high-quality primary healthcare services while supporting the education and training of the next generation of health professionals. Based at Warwick, we are seeking a Dental Assistant to support students and staff in delivering exceptional patient care. Key responsibilities for this role will include: Assist staff and students across a broad range of dental treatments and procedures. Prepare patients for treatment and support clinic operations, working autonomously and using initiative to manage day-to-day responsibilities effectively. Maintain clinical hygiene and adhere to infection control protocols. Provide administrative and reception support. Uphold university values and comply with policies, health and safety requirements, and professional About you \nTo be successful in this role, you will hold: An Australian Dental Assistant qualification or recognised equivalent is highly desirable. Current CPR/First Aid Certification from a recognised provider. Current Queensland Blue Card (or willingness to obtain). In addition to the above, you will demonstrate: Excellent teamwork and communication skills. Ability to work under supervision and contribute to efficient clinic operations. Strong administrative skills with attention to detail. A commitment to patient care and student learning. What we can offer \nThis is a full-time, fixed-term position until October 2027, based primarily at Griffith University’s Warwick location. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 4 range $76,126 - $80,321 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $89,067 - $93,976 per annum. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description )  Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact the Dental Clinic Manager at  dentalclinicmanager@griffith.edu.au . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner at j.dhall@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Wednesday, 16 September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146885524": {
      "title": "Privacy Compliance Manager",
      "description": "About the Opportunity The Privacy Compliance Manager leads the University’s privacy compliance program through consultative and constructive interaction with element leadership, managers, and liaisons. Success depends on a risk-based approach to define priorities, a commitment to foster strong relationships, open communication towards stakeholders, and dedication to cultivating behaviours and actions that uphold and reinforce integrity, accountability and transparency Key Responsibilities Oversee and manage Right to Information (RTI), administrative access, and related privacy complaints. Conduct and supervise investigations into RTI, administrative access matters and privacy complaints; identify and resolve systemic privacy issues in collaboration with University staff. Lead the development and delivery of privacy education, training, and awareness programs. Monitor legislative changes and update University policies, procedures, and templates accordingly. Support the University’s privacy compliance program and assist the Privacy Officer with RTI, administrative access and complaint matters. Maintain and report statistics on RTI, administrative access and privacy complaints to internal and external stakeholders. Liaise with regulatory bodies during compliance reviews and investigations. Develop and implement a risk-based privacy compliance program aligned with University strategy and legal requirements. Guide continuous improvement of the University's privacy compliance framework in collaboration with stakeholders. Advise senior leadership on privacy obligations, including data mapping, risk assessments and privacy impact assessments. Support internal audits and advise privacy champions across the University. Promote accountability by advising on and monitoring corrective actions. Represent privacy interests in University committees and working groups to enhance privacy practices. Provide regular updates and reports to senior management and the Audit & Risk Committee on compliance progress. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant postgraduate qualifications (preferably legal qualifications) with at least five (5) years-experience in a similar role or have an equivalent level of expertise obtained from a combination of experience, training, professional accreditation and qualification. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and may be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer \n \nThis is a full time, continuing opportunity primarily based Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 10 - Base salary of $147,057.74 + 17% super. Full package $172,057.55. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description.  Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acqusition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 20th September 2026  at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "General Counsel"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146877759": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarship: Responsible Infrastructure for Agentic AI Systems",
      "description": "We are currently looking for a PhD candidate to investigate the responsible design, evaluation, and governance of infrastructure for agentic AI systems .  The primary focus of this role is to develop methods that improve the reliability, accountability, and resilience of shared runtime components used by autonomous and multi-agent AI systems .  This project includes research on agent memory, shared state, tool-use workflows, retrieval-augmented generation, context management, and runtime monitoring mechanisms .  Success in this role requires collaboration with academic researchers, industry partners, and interdisciplinary stakeholders working on trustworthy AI, software systems, and emerging digital infrastructure. This project is embedded in an ARC Linkage Project, offering the candidate opportunities to work with academic and industry partners on responsible infrastructure for next-generation agentic AI systems. \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful within this role, you will be able to demonstrate strong analytical, programming, and problem-solving skills, with the capacity to conduct independent research in AI systems, software infrastructure, and responsible technology development. You will have evidence of a passion for agentic AI, trustworthy AI, multi-agent systems, and intelligent software infrastructure, with a strong desire to undertake research in [responsible infrastructure for agentic AI systems. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to  first-class honours , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Policy . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program, refer  here . Please note : Applicants should have a strong background in Information Technology, Computer Science, Mathematics, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related discipline. Applicants should have a strong academic record, normally with a GPA greater than 85/100 or equivalent. Applicants with prior research experience, research project involvement, peer-reviewed publications, or demonstrated experience in AI, machine learning, software systems, multi-agent systems, or related areas will be highly regarded. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 OR A score of no less than 3+ in each skill of the ISLPR (conducted by ISLPR Language Services only) OR A minimum overall score of 176 (no score less than 169) on C1 Advanced  or  C2 Proficiency OR An overall score of 58 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 50 (applies to tests taken prior to 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 55 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 47 (applies to tests taken on or after 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 70 in the LanguageCert Academic OR An overall score of 59 in the Michigan English Test (MET) . \n\n About the scholarship The 2026 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $35,656 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the  GUPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years full time study. Please see the  GUIPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EoI process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  leo.zhang@griffith.edu.au  containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Brief research proposal, maximum 2 pages Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the ‘About you’ section A curriculum vitae (CV) using the  Griffith CV template . Names and contact details of two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is: Friday 02 October 2026 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line \n \n Further information For project related enquiries please contact: \nProfessor Leo Zhang \nPhone: (07) 5552 8834 \nEmail:   leo.zhang@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n The project will be undertaken within the School of Information and Communication Technology at Griffith University, in connection with the TrustAGI research lab. The lab conducts research on trustworthy and responsible artificial intelligence, with interests spanning agentic AI systems, multi-agent coordination, AI governance, software systems, and emerging digital infrastructure. This opportunity will be primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146861784": {
      "error": "not present in bulk fetch result"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146615724": {
      "title": "Technical Officer ",
      "description": "About the Opportunity  We are seeking a skilled Technical Officer to support the delivery of teaching and research outcomes within our mechanical workshop facilities. Working under the direction of the Manager or Lead Technical Officer, you will manufacture, maintain and repair specialised equipment, provide technical guidance to staff and students, and ensure workshop operations are safe, efficient and compliant. This is an excellent opportunity to apply your technical expertise in a collaborative environment that supports innovation, learning and research excellence. Key responsibilities Support teaching, research and consultancy activities through the manufacture, modification, maintenance and repair of mechanical equipment and components. Interpret technical drawings and specifications to fabricate, machine and weld specialised equipment. Provide technical advice and hands-on support to staff and students in the design and development of equipment and prototypes. Diagnose faults and perform maintenance and repairs on workshop and University equipment. Deliver training and guidance on the safe use of workshop tools, machinery and processes. Maintain workshop records, inventory and procurement activities to ensure efficient operations. Contribute to a safe, compliant and continuously improving workshop environment. Provide excellent customer service and collaborate effectively with colleagues across Technical Services and the Sciences Group. Undertake other duties consistent with the level and responsibilities of the role. About you The occupant of this position will hold a recognised trade qualification in fitting and turning, mechanical engineering trades, metal fabrication, or a related discipline, together with demonstrated experience in the operation of workshop machinery and fabrication equipment, including lathes, milling machines, saws, grinders, presses and welding equipment. Alternatively, an equivalent combination of relevant qualifications, training and practical experience may be considered. What we can offer \nThis is a full time continuing opportunity primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 5 – Base range - $82,415.66 - $92,456.55 + 17% super. Full package range - $96,426.31 - $108,174.16. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 20th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. (please note advertising for this role has been extended, all previous applicants are still being considered) \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Griffith Sciences"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146616279": {
      "title": "Mechanical Workshop Technical Lead",
      "description": "About the Opportunity  Lead the Mechanical Workshop team in delivering high-quality mechanical assembly, fabrication, welding, and machining services that support research, teaching, and external projects. Using a range of workshop equipment, including lathes, milling machines, water-jet cutters, and welding equipment, you will provide technical expertise, coordinate resources and priorities, and work closely with the Workshop Manager to ensure successful project delivery. Key responsibilities Provide technical guidance to the Workshops Manager on equipment, maintenance, training, and operational matters. Plan and deliver fabrication, repair, and engineering projects, from procurement through to completion. Oversee daily workshop operations, ensuring safe, efficient, and high-quality service delivery. Work with clients to define project requirements, timelines, and outcomes. Support the scheduling, prioritisation, and allocation of workshop resources. Lead and mentor the Mechanical Workshop team, maintaining quality standards and resolving technical issues. Drive continuous improvement initiatives to enhance workshop performance and efficiency. Promote a safe, professional, and well-organised workshop environment. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant tertiary qualifications and subsequent relevant experience or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Demonstrated competency in tig welding skill of both aluminium and stainless steel. This role also involves working with a range of materials, including metals, plastics, timber, and composites, and the operation of workshop equipment used for manufacturing, machining, fabrication, assembly, and prototyping activities. Experience across these broader technical functions, particularly in the operation of CNC manufacturing equipment and associated technologies, would be highly regarded. What we can offer \nThis is a continuing position primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 7 – base range $104,504.60 - $113,219.43 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $122,270.38 - $132,466.72. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 20th September at 11:59pm.  All applications must be submitted online. \n \n (please note advertising for this role has been extended, all previous applicants are still being considered) \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Griffith Sciences"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146615239": {
      "title": "Centre Manager, Griffith Head and Neck Centre",
      "description": "About the opportunity  \nThe Griffith Head and Neck Centre is a newly established joint clinical academic centre of Griffith University and Gold Coast Hospital and Health Service, supported during its founding period by the Garnett Passe and Rodney Williams Memorial Foundation. The Centre brings together clinicians, researchers, educators, scientists, engineers, consumers and industry partners to improve care for people with disorders of the head and neck.   We are seeking an experienced and entrepreneurial Centre Manager to help build the Centre during its formative years. Working closely with the founding Director, Professor Jason Fleming, you will play a central role in establishing the Centre’s operational foundations while helping shape its long-term growth, partnerships and sustainability. This is a unique and exciting opportunity to contribute to the development of a new clinical academic centre with genuine scope to influence its direction from the outset. This is not a research position, nor is it a traditional administrative role. Dedicated administrative support is provided separately, allowing the Centre Manager to focus on strategic operations, partnership development, governance, business development and program delivery.   About the role \nAs Centre Manager you will: Support delivery of the Centre’s strategic priorities, business planning and governance; Develop partnerships with industry, philanthropy, government and academic collaborators; Coordinate the Centre’s programs, initiatives and major projects; Oversee financial planning, reporting and performance monitoring; Build productive relationships across Griffith University, Gold Coast Hospital and Health Service and external partners; and Contribute to the long-term growth and sustainability of the Centre. This is a part-time (0.5 FTE), fixed-term appointment for five years based at Griffith University’s Gold Coast location. As Griffith University is a multi-campus institution you may be required to work at other campuses or other sites on occasion. The position is classified at professional staff HEW 8 level, and the step at which the successful candidate is appointed will depend on their educational and professional background. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 8 range $117,579 - $132,273 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $137,567 - $154,759 per annum. Why join us? \nThis is a rare opportunity to help establish a new multidisciplinary clinical academic centre from its inception. You will work directly with senior academic, clinical and external partners while contributing to research, education and innovation with the potential to improve patient care across Queensland and beyond. You’ll join a supportive team within the School of Medicine and Dentistry and Griffith Health and enjoy the flexibility, professional development opportunities and employment benefits offered by Griffith University. \n\n We are seeking applications from experienced professionals who enjoy building organisations and working across strategy, partnerships and operations. The successful candidate will bring: Experience in strategic operations, program management, research development, partnerships or business development within a university, health, research or not-for-profit environment; Demonstrated ability to develop productive stakeholder relationships across complex organisations; Strong organisational, financial and project management skills; Excellent written and verbal communication; Sound judgement, initiative and the ability to work independently within a newly established environment; and A collaborative approach with a genuine interest in supporting research, education and innovation. Experience working within universities, health services, medical research institutes, or advancement environments will be highly regarded. We are seeking candidates who possess a relevant degree with subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education/training. Further eligibility requirements are contained in the Position Description which is accessible below.  \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: 50% fee discount for work related post graduate Griffith degrees Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission). Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Jason Fleming via email at: j.fleming@griffith.edu.au . For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner on  j.dhall@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Monday, 21 September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The  School of Medicine and Dentistry  strives to prepare the next generation of professionals and practitioners to tackle health and healthcare challenges in an ever-changing world. As a community, we are committed to building better health outcomes for all by delivering high-quality education, impactful research and engagement with and for the communities we serve. As articulated in our Strategic Plan, we commit to the University's values and, importantly, to being a School for Country, place, communities and the people we serve. Through our learning and teaching, we strive to produce graduates who are confident, competent and resilient to be agents for change.  We are committed to recruiting and retaining the best possible staff; staff who support our mission and vision. The School of Medicine and Dentistry shares the Health Group and broader University's commitment to excellence, ethical behaviour, and engagement. The Health Group Charter articulates the core values and behaviours we expect in our workforce: inclusion, integrity, performance, respect, and collaboration.  These values and behaviours are embedded in the School's annual Academic Employee Career Development (AECD) / Professional Staff Career Development (PSCD) process and frame staff performance planning and review conversations.",
      "department": "School of Medicine and Dentistry"
    },
