    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146393550": {
      "title": "Head of Strategic Procurement",
      "description": "About the Opportunity  The Head of Strategic Procurement is a key leadership role within the Finance team, responsible for driving the University's procurement strategy and delivering a high-performing, value-focused procurement function. Leading a team of procurement professionals, the role will enhance procurement governance, streamline processes, and improve the stakeholder experience while ensuring commercially sound, transparent, and compliant procurement outcomes. Operating within a centre-led, decentralised procurement model, the Head of Strategic Procurement will provide expert advice to senior stakeholders, drive procurement excellence and efficiencies, and foster a strong customer-focused approach. The role also ensures the University meets its regulatory, financial, ethical, sustainability, modern slavery, risk, and responsible procurement obligations, supporting the achievement of the University's broader strategic objectives. Key Responsibilities Lead the University’s procurement function, delivering efficient, value-driven procurement services aligned to strategic and operational priorities. Drive procurement governance, risk management, compliance, and assurance frameworks to support transparent and accountable decision-making. Develop and implement procurement strategies, category management approaches, and contract management practices that maximise value, strengthen supplier performance, and reduce complexity. Simplify procurement processes and systems to enhance stakeholder experience, improve efficiency, and provide responsive support. Provide expert procurement, commercial, and governance advice to senior leaders and key stakeholders. Manage the procurement pipeline, ensuring effective prioritisation, planning, and delivery of strategic procurement activities. Build strong stakeholder and supplier relationships to deliver practical solutions and sustainable commercial outcomes. Lead, develop, and empower a high-performing procurement team, fostering accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Promote innovation, digital enablement, ethical procurement practices, and compliance with relevant legislation, policies, and governance requirements. Represent the University in engagement with government, suppliers, industry networks, and external partners. About you Extensive leadership experience in strategic procurement, sourcing, contract management, and supplier governance within complex organisations. Proven ability to lead a centre-led procurement function, delivering strong governance, stakeholder outcomes, and measurable value. Strong commercial acumen with the ability to use data and insights to inform strategy and decision-making. Excellent stakeholder engagement, influencing, and negotiation skills, with success managing complex commercial matters. Sound knowledge of procurement governance, risk, compliance, probity, and contract management. Commitment to sustainable, ethical, and responsible procurement practices. Demonstrated success leading teams, driving change, and building a high-performance culture. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and may be subject to a National criminal history check. Sponsorship is not available for this role.  What we can offer \nThis is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 5 years primarily based Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary A competitive salary will be negotiated with the preferred candidate. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 13th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. We kindly ask recruitment agencies not to send unsolicited CVs or approach members of our hiring team regarding this role, as the recruitment process is being managed internally. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Finance"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146393660": {
      "title": "Head of Financial Control",
      "description": "About the Opportunity  As a key member of the Finance Senior Leadership Team, this role provides strategic leadership across financial reporting, financial control, treasury, tax, financial assurance, and research accounting functions. Reporting to the CFO, the Head of Financial Control delivers trusted financial advice to senior executives, supports informed decision-making, and ensures strong governance, compliance, and financial stewardship across the University. Leading a diverse team, the role is responsible for statutory financial reporting, treasury management, including a significant investment portfolio, and maintaining a robust financial control environment. The position also drives continuous improvement, strengthens financial systems and processes, and fosters a high-performance culture that supports the University's strategic objectives. As a critical leadership role, the incumbent plays a key part in safeguarding the University's fraud and corruption control framework, ensuring effective governance, risk management, and financial integrity across the institution. Key Responsibilities Lead and develop high-performing teams across Financial Management, Treasury, Tax, Financial Assurance, and Research Accounting. Foster a collaborative, customer-focused culture that drives excellence, innovation, and continuous improvement. Provide strategic leadership, coaching, and direction while building strong relationships across the University. Oversee the University's financial control framework, ensuring compliance with accounting standards, legislation, and internal policies. Lead statutory financial reporting, audit management, financial assurance activities, and governance reporting. Maintain the integrity, accuracy, and reliability of the University's financial systems, processes, and reporting. Partner with senior executives to provide expert advice on complex financial, accounting, treasury, tax, and commercial matters. Lead treasury operations, including investment, cashflow, borrowing, and balance sheet management. Manage key external relationships, including auditors, banking and investment partners, and professional advisors. Support strategic initiatives and special projects that contribute to the University's long-term success. Strengthen financial risk management, fraud prevention, and assurance frameworks across the University. Ensure a robust control environment that supports sound decision-making, accountability, and financial sustainability. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant tertiary qualifications, preferably at postgraduate level, and substantial relevant work experience.  Membership of a professional accredited accounting organisation such as CA,or CPA  is mandatory. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and may be subject to a National criminal history check. Sponsorship is not available for this role.  What we can offer \nThis is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 5 years primarily based Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary A competitive salary will be negotiated with the preferred candidate. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 13th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. We kindly ask recruitment agencies not to send unsolicited CVs or approach members of our hiring team regarding this role, as the recruitment process is being managed internally. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Finance"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146393489": {
      "title": "Director, Griffith Asia Institute",
      "description": "As Director, Griffith Asia Institute, you will shape the Institute’s next chapter—setting its strategic direction, leading its globally connected research community and advancing its ambition for Asia and the Pacific to lead the world in sustainable development. You will champion interdisciplinary research and expand GAI’s influence in policy, practice and public debate. Reporting to the Dean (Research), you will align GAI’s priorities with the research and engagement ambitions of Griffith Business School and the wider University. You will lead and support a high-performing community of researchers and professional staff, oversee governance and resources, and grow and diversify external funding, research, education and capacity-building opportunities. As a visible ambassador for GAI, you will deepen strategic relationships with universities, governments, industry, donors and communities across Asia and the Pacific. You will translate the Institute’s regional expertise into meaningful impact and position Griffith as a trusted partner on the issues shaping the region’s future. About you You are an internationally respected academic leader with the vision and collaborative style to guide GAI’s next phase. You bring a doctoral qualification and significant national and international standing, deep Asia-Pacific expertise, a strong record of research and thought leadership, and experience leading a prominent institute, centre or complex academic enterprise. Associate Professor (Level D) and Professor (Level E) are encouraged to apply. You will demonstrate: Inspiring and inclusive leadership, with a record of developing people and building high-performing teams. Strong regional networks and the cultural capability to build trusted partnerships across sectors and borders. Success translating interdisciplinary research into policy, practice and public debate. A proven ability to secure and diversify external funding and income. Sound strategic, governance and resource-management capability. What we can offer This is a fixed-term (for five years), full-time position and you will be primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. Please note that Griffith Business School at Brisbane South (Nathan) will be relocating to Griffith CBD, with an intended relocation date of early 2027. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations   \n\n A doctoral qualification in a discipline related to the Institute \n\n Why Griffith? At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply \nPlease submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the Job Description/Key Accountabilities above and the  position description ). Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details. Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Visa sponsorship may be available to the successful candidate. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Chris Fleming, Dean Research, Griffith Business School, via email: chris.fleming@griffith.edu.au. For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Kate Watson, Talent Acquisition Partner via email: kate.watson@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Thursday 1st October,  at 11:59 pm AEST All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 2 – 3 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Griffith Asia Institute (GAI) is an internationally recognised research centre within Griffith Business School. GAI reflects Griffith University's enduring commitment to the study and engagement of nations in Asia and the Pacific. Propelling Asia and the Pacific to become global leaders in sustainable development. Building on this strong foundation, GAI brings world-class expertise to the defining challenges and opportunities shaping Asia and the Pacific. Through ambitious interdisciplinary research, influential regional partnerships and evidence-based engagement, the Institute connects ideas with action across government, business, academia and communities. For an incoming Director, this is a rare opportunity to lead an established, high-impact institute and strengthen its voice, reach and influence at a pivotal time for the region.",
      "department": "Griffith Business School"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146120279": {
      "title": "Head of Department, Department of Management",
      "description": "As Head of Department, Department of Management, you will lead a thriving academic department to strengthen impactful research, deepen industry connections, and pursue outstanding student outcomes. Reporting to the Dean (Academic), you will provide strategic direction and leadership across teaching, research, engagement and people management, ensuring the ongoing success and growth. You will cultivate an environment that encourages innovation, collaboration and academic achievement, while driving initiatives that strengthen the Department of Management’s reputation, performance and contribution to Griffith University’s strategic objectives. About you As an accomplished academic leader in Management or a related field, you have a demonstrated history of advancing excellence in teaching, research and external engagement. You possess the strategic insight, leadership expertise and collaborative mindset required to guide a multidisciplinary academic department and inspire outstanding outcomes across people, programs and partnerships. A skilled and influential communicator, you establish strong relationships with academic colleagues, students, industry stakeholders, professional associations and community partners. You bring experience leading complex teams and overseeing budgets and resources, and you are committed to fostering a supportive, high-performing culture in a dynamic and evolving environment. To be successful in this role, you will also possess: A doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent accreditation and standing A strong record of achievement in learning and teaching, research and/or industry engagement Proven experience managing people, performance, budgets and resources to achieve strategic objectives The ability to drive innovation, foster collaboration and lead organisational change Excellent communication, influencing and stakeholder engagement skills A commitment to academic excellence, integrity, equity, diversity and inclusion Most importantly, you will be a values-led leader who can inspire others, champion continuous improvement and contribute to Griffith University's reputation as a leading institution for education, research and community impact. What we can offer The successful candidate will be appointed as Head of Department, Department Management on an initial fixed-term, five-year senior contract and will hold an ongoing, continuing substantive appointment at a Professorial level. You may be primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. Please note that Griffith Business School at Brisbane South (Nathan) will be relocating to Griffith CBD, with an intended relocation date of February 2027.  As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nA competitive salary will be negotiated with the successful candidate. \n\n As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. You will enjoy: Generous superannuation and leave provisions. Access to health and wellbeing programs, fitness facilities and employee assistance services. How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information, please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Visa sponsorship may be available to the successful candidate. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Martin Berka, Dean (Academic), Griffith Business School via gbsdeanacademic@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, please contact Kate Watson, Talent Acquisition Partner via kate.watson@griffith.edu.au Closing date:  Wednesday 30th September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 2 – 3 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The Department of Management brings together leading expertise in business innovation, entrepreneurship, health services management, employment relations and human resources, delivering a globally recognised and industry-relevant education. Emphasising sustainability, adaptability, diversity and ethics, we prepare students to lead and succeed in evolving business environments across the Asia-Pacific region and beyond. Recognised as Australia's leading research institution in Strategic Management ( The Australian 2026 Research Magazine ), the Department influences policy, business practice and regulation while equipping graduates to address complex local and global challenges. Through strong industry engagement and innovative teaching, we develop the skills, knowledge and connections needed to create lasting business impact. In addition, scheduled to open in the not-too-distant future, our new location,  our heritage-listed Treasury Building in Brisbane’s CBD, represents an exciting, fresh chapter for the University and our students.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146119619": {
      "title": "Head of Department, Tourism and Marketing",
      "description": "As Head of Department, Tourism and Marketing, you will provide strategic leadership to a high-performing academic community renowned for its impact-driven research, industry partnerships and commitment to student success. Reporting to the Dean (Academic), you will shape the direction of the Department, driving excellence across teaching, research, external engagement and people leadership. This is a unique opportunity to influence the future of two dynamic and globally connected disciplines. You will foster a culture of innovation, collaboration and academic excellence while leading strategic initiatives that enhance the Department's reputation, performance and contribution to Griffith University's vision. Working closely with colleagues across the Griffith Business School and the wider University, you will champion high-quality learning experiences, support research growth and translation, strengthen industry and community partnerships, and ensure the effective stewardship of resources to achieve ambitious strategic goals. About you \nAs a respected academic leader in a Marketing or Tourism (or related) discipline with a strong track record of fostering excellence in teaching, research and external engagement, you bring the strategic vision, leadership capability and collaborative approach needed to lead a diverse academic department and inspire high performance across people, programs and partnerships. You are an effective relationship builder, able to engage confidently with colleagues, students, industry partners, professional bodies and the broader community. With experience leading complex teams and managing significant resources, you thrive in a dynamic environment and are passionate about creating a positive, inclusive and high-performing culture. To be successful in this role, you will possess: A doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent accreditation and standing Demonstrated leadership experience within higher education or a similarly complex organisation A strong record of achievement in learning and teaching, research and/or industry engagement Proven experience managing people, budgets and resources to achieve strategic objectives The ability to drive innovation, foster collaboration and lead organisational change Excellent communication, influencing and stakeholder engagement skills A commitment to academic excellence, integrity, equity, diversity and inclusion Most importantly, you will be a values-led leader who can inspire others, champion continuous improvement and contribute to Griffith University's reputation as a leading institution for education, research and community impact. What we can offer The successful candidate will be appointed as Head of Department, Department of Tourism and Marketing on an initial fixed-term, five-year senior contract and will hold an ongoing, continuing substantive appointment at a Professorial level. You may be primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. Please note that Griffith Business School at Brisbane South (Nathan) will be relocating to Griffith CBD, with an intended relocation date of February 2027.  As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nA competitive salary will be negotiated with the successful candidate. \n\n At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information, please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Visa sponsorship may be available to the successful candidate. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Martin Berka, Dean (Academic), Griffith Business School via gbsdeanacademic@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, please contact Kate Watson, Talent Acquisition Partner via kate.watson@griffith.edu.au Closing date:  Wednesday 30th September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 2 – 3 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Our Department of Tourism and Marketing combines the expertise of world-renowned academic staff to deliver an unmatched educational experience. Our internationally recognised degrees bring together industry-relevant content, cutting-edge research and strong partnerships. We are recognized as Australia's top research institution in Marketing as well as Hospitality and Tourism ( 2026 Australian Research Magazine ) and ranked 6th globally and 1st in Australia for Hospitality and Tourism in the  ShanghaiRanking (GRAS), 2025. In addition, scheduled to open in the not-too-distant future, our new location,  our heritage-listed Treasury Building in Brisbane’s CBD, represents an exciting, fresh chapter for the University and our students.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146111059": {
      "title": "Timetabling Services Officer",
      "description": "Functioning within Student Life, the Exams and Timetabling team specifically provides operational and administrative support and services to academic elements and students for all class timetabling, examination management, grade publication and student progression processes as well as assessment applications and room bookings. Working with the Timetabling Services team, you’ll be responsible for class timetabling for a group of schools, as well as supporting full class management and room bookings. Key Responsibilities Build and maintain strong, trusted relationships with academic and professional staff Deliver accurate class timetabling and room booking outcomes within agreed timeframes Independently resolve complex scheduling issues using specialised timetabling systems Develop optimal scheduling solutions aligned with University policies and priorities Ensure efficient and effective use of teaching spaces and facilities Identify, recommend, and implement opportunities to streamline, improve, and automate processes Contribute to an enhanced student and staff experience through service excellence About you To be successful in the role you will have the demonstrated ability to: Experience in timetabling, scheduling, space management, or a similar coordination role Demonstrated ability to manage complex data and competing priorities with high attention to detail Proven stakeholder engagement skills, with confidence working with academic staff Strong analytical and problem‑solving capability, including system‑based troubleshooting Experience using complex systems and databases (timetabling or scheduling systems highly regarded) Ability to work autonomously while contributing effectively to a collaborative team Continuous improvement mindset with a focus on efficiency and service quality What We Can Offer This is a fixed-term (12 months), full-time position primarily based at our Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University, you will be required to work across other locations. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary will be in the range HEW Level 6: $94,966 – $101,295 p.a. + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range of  $111,110 – $118,515 per annum. \n\n Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter (no longer than 2 pages) outlining your suitability for the role referring to the key responsibilities in the  Position Description Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details. Applicants must have Australian working rights and successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Caroline Carlish, Manager, Timetabling Services, via email c.carlish@griffith.edu.au Closing date:  Sunday 13th September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 3 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Fixed Term (12 months), Full-time opportunity within Student and Academic Services Brisbane South (Nathan) based",
      "department": "Student Life"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146095519": {
      "title": "School Manager - School of Nursing and Midwifery",
      "description": "The School of Nursing and Midwifery is currently recruiting a passionate and dedicated School Manager to join the team of senior administrative staff within the Health Group. This role will ensure the quality and consistency of high service delivery as well as support positive teaching and student experiences across a large school.  \n  \nThe School Manager is the primary advisor to the Head of School and School Executive on all matters pertaining to the University, Group and School policies, operations, and business processes.  Key responsibilities include:  Providing high level advice and support to the Head of School and other senior staff.  Support with planning, budgeting, resource management and other operational matters along with external engagement activities.  Assist with academic work allocation.  Lead business improvement and change processes.  Manage and lead School professional staff.  The position actively participates as a member of the School Executive and plays a key role in contributing to the strategic and operational objectives of the School and Group.  About you \nTo be successful in this position, you will hold relevant tertiary qualifications and evidence of extensive management experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training.  In addition to the above, you will demonstrate:  A strategic thinker, with a track record of developing and maintaining strong relationships.  A collaborative team member with proven expertise in leading an administrative team in a high-pressure environment.  Excellent written and verbal communication skills with experience in the preparation of briefings, information papers, budget and other reports.  Project management and/or business process improvement experience, with an ability to partner with colleagues to overcome complex matters in short timeframes.  Knowledge and/or experience in the contemporary challenges facing the higher education sector.  Sound understanding of financial matters including high level reporting.  What we can offer \nThis is a continuing, full-time position primarily based at Griffith University’s Gold Coast campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. HEW level 9 salary range $137,165 - $142,070 per annum, plus 17% superannuation.  \n\n Why join Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description )  Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner ,  Head of School  on  hos.sonm@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, please contact Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at m.mahon@griffith.edu.au . Closing date:  11:59pm AEST 18 September. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "School of Nursing and Midwifery"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146083159": {
      "title": "Research Support Officer",
      "description": "We are seeking a highly organised and motivated Research Support Officer to join the Griffith Business School Research Operations Team. Reporting to the Research Support Manager within the Dean (Research) Office, this position provides professional administrative and operational support for research activities across Griffith Business School. As a shared resource, the Research Support Officer may support activities at Group, Department or Research Entity level. Working under broad direction, the Research Support Officer is responsible for a varied portfolio of research operations, communications, events, projects, systems and administrative processes. The role supports the effective delivery and promotion of the School’s research activities, profile and impact. It is a professional staff position focused on enabling research operations rather than undertaking academic research. Key responsibilities will include: Coordinate operational, administrative and project activities for the Research Operations Team, researchers, committees and working groups, including preparing meeting papers and minutes, tracking action items and supporting agreed outcomes. Develop communications that promote GBS research and impact to internal and external audiences, including LinkedIn articles, research stories, web and intranet content, and other promotional material. Plan and coordinate research events, workshops, seminars and stakeholder engagement activities, managing timelines, communications, logistics and follow-up to support effective delivery. Coordinate the administration of small grant schemes and programs, including application rounds, submissions and records, assessment processes, applicant communications and outcome reporting. Coordinate administrative processes relating to projects, finance and HR, including payments, invoicing, small budgets, routine correspondence and record management, in accordance with relevant University requirements. Gather, prepare and analyse research data, including publications and research income, for meetings, dashboards and reporting. Maintain accurate and up-to-date records for the Research Operations Team. Maintain and support research information and profile platforms, including Symplectic Elements and Griffith Experts, to ensure the accuracy and visibility of GBS research information. Contribute to the delivery and promotion of strategic research programs and initiatives across Griffith Business School, its departments and research entities. Build effective working relationships with academic and professional staff, central University areas and external stakeholders, and use sound judgement to resolve routine matters or escalate issues where appropriate. About you Experience developing research communications, including research stories, academic profiles, website content and social media content. Experience coordinating research seminars, workshops, conferences and stakeholder engagement activities. Experience supporting research teams, research centres, institutes or academic departments including coordinating research-related committees or working groups and preparing research reports & briefing papers to support.  In addition you will have: Highly developed skills in coordinating professional administrative, operational or project activities, with the ability to organise competing priorities and deliver accurate work within agreed timeframes. Strong written communication skills, including the ability to prepare clear and engaging content for different audiences and communication channels. Strong interpersonal and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to build positive working relationships and communicate effectively with people at different levels. Experience gathering, maintaining and presenting information for reporting, meetings or decision-making, with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. A positive, friendly and team-oriented approach, with a genuine willingness to assist others, share responsibilities and contribute to a supportive and collaborative working environment. What we can offer This is a full-time continuing position based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan). From February 2027 (the anticipated relocation date), your primary work location will be Brisbane CBD – the date of the relocation is yet to be confirmed. As a multi-site university, Griffith may also require work across other locations as needed. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 6 range $94,966 - $101,295 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $111,110 - $118,515 per annum. \n\n At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please note : This position was recently advertised (June 2026) and as such, applicants who have previously applied for this position will not be required to submit a further application. Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the \"About you\", above and the  position description ). If applying through the Indeed jobs board, please include your cover letter in your resume document. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details. Applicants must have Australian working rights. Sponsorship is not offered and successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Khyla Truloff, via email: k.truloff@griffith.edu.au. Closing date:  Sunday, 13th September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Pro Vice Chancellor (Business)"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000146082279": {
      "title": "Global Mobility Adviser (Inbound) - Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast ",
      "description": "About the Opportunity The Global Mobility Adviser (Inbound) plays a key role in supporting Study Abroad and Exchange students throughout their mobility journey at Griffith, enabling them to successfully complete a non-award trimester or year-long study program. The role involves engaging with incoming students from pre-arrival through to program completion, while contributing to the promotion, administration and continuous improvement of inbound mobility programs. Key responsibilities Provide guidance and support to inbound Study Abroad and Exchange students considering non-award study opportunities at Griffith through a range of communication channels, working collaboratively with stakeholders to promote programs and increase student participation. Assist with the administration and processing of applications for inbound mobility for exchange and study abroad programs. Represent Griffith Global Mobility at events, information sessions, expos, Open Day and visits from partner institutions, agents and government delegates. Develop and maintain website content and support the creation of promotional materials to enhance student engagement and participation. Maintain accurate mobility data and records, and prepare reports and statistics as required. Keep current with relevant legislation, regulatory requirements, University policies and emerging trends in international education and student mobility. About you We are seeking a highly organised and student-focused professional who is passionate about international education and delivering exceptional service. The successful candidate will demonstrate: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to confidently engage with students, staff and external stakeholders. Strong presentation and public speaking skills, including experience delivering information sessions, presentations and promotional activities to diverse audiences. Exceptional administrative skills, with a high level of accuracy, attention to detail and the ability to manage complex processes and competing priorities. A customer-focused approach and genuine commitment to supporting students throughout their global learning experiences. Experience developing, maintaining or promoting content across digital and print channels, including websites, presentations, brochures and other marketing materials. Strong digital literacy and the ability to quickly learn and work across a range of systems and platforms. The ability to work collaboratively as part of a team while taking ownership of tasks and delivering outcomes in a fast-paced environment. Applicant must have full unrestricted work rights for Australia and will be subject to a national criminal history check.  What we can offer \nThis is a full time , continuing position and can be based at Griffith University Gold Coast or Brisbane South (Nathan) campuses. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary  \nHEW 5 – Base range salary - $82,415.66 - $92,456.55 +17% superannuation. Full package range - $96,426.31 - $108,174.16.  \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 13th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You will find we are about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you will achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "International Office"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000145902297": {
      "title": "Clinic Support Officer",
      "description": "Griffith Health is seeking a motivated and customer-focused Clinic Support Officer to join our clinic team. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment and is passionate about delivering high-quality administrative and client support within a healthcare setting. Reporting to the Reception Team Leader, you will play a key role in ensuring the smooth day-to-day operation of the clinic. As the first point of contact, you will provide professional reception and administrative support to patients, students, and staff, while contributing to a positive and efficient clinic experience. Key Responsibilities Provide exceptional front-line customer service via phone, email, and in person Manage patient enquiries and resolve routine matters, escalating when required Coordinate patient bookings and maintain accurate scheduling records Process payments and perform daily financial reconciliation and reporting Maintain and update clinic systems, records, and databases Assist with patient record management, including documentation and results handling Support general administrative functions, reporting, and correspondence Collaborate with clinic staff to support service delivery and operations About You \nYou are an organised and detail-oriented professional with strong communication skills and a commitment to excellent client service. You will bring: An associate diploma qualification or equivalent relevant experience Experience in administrative or reception roles, ideally within a healthcare or clinic environment Strong organisational and time management skills Confidence using digital systems and databases The ability to handle sensitive information with confidentiality and professionalism A proactive approach and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team A strong client focus, excellent presentation, and a demonstrated ability to contribute effectively within a team environment. What we can offer \nThis is a continuing, full-time position based at the Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 4 range $76,126 - $80,321 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $89,067 - $93,976 per annum. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact the Dental Clinic Manager at  dentalclinicmanager@griffith.edu.au . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner at j.dhall@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Thursday, 10 September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": ""
