    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000145417859": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Level B) in Nutrition and Dietetics",
      "description": "The  School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work  is known for leadership and excellence in health education, research, and clinical practice, with a commitment to developing work-ready graduates.  With programs spanning Physiotherapy, Social Work, Nutrition and Dietetics, Exercise Science, Occupational Therapy, and Speech Pathology, we bring together a diverse team of academics who are pioneering change in their fields.  As a Lecturer in Nutrition and Dietetics , you will play an important role in developing knowledgeable, capable and compassionate health professionals. Through innovative teaching, authentic assessment and strong industry connections, you will help students translate evidence into practice and prepare them to respond to evolving health and workforce needs. Key aspects of the role include: Delivering contemporary learning experiences informed by professional practice and emerging evidence. Guiding and supporting students throughout their academic and professional development. Coordinating courses and contributing to a cohesive, high quality program experience. Developing partnerships that expand practical learning and graduate employment opportunities. Collaborating with colleagues to strengthen teaching quality, scholarship and the School’s profile. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. \n\n To be successful in this role, you will bring strong discipline knowledge, a passion for student learning and the ability to connect contemporary evidence with professional practice. You will also demonstrate a collaborative approach and a commitment to delivering an inclusive and high quality student experience. You will have: A doctoral or master’s qualification in nutrition and/or dietetics,  the credential of Accredited Practising Dietitian (APD) or eligibility to become accredited as a dietitian in Australia, and substantial professional experience. Demonstrated experience in teaching, training or supporting learning in a university, clinical or professional environment. Contemporary knowledge of nutrition and dietetics practice, with the ability to translate evidence into engaging learning experiences. Strong communication, collaboration and organisational skills, including the capacity to coordinate courses and academic activities. A commitment to reflective practice, educational innovation and the continuous improvement of student outcomes. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Rozanne Kruger, Professor in Nutrition and Dietetics within School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work at r.kruger@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, please contact Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at m.mahon@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Monday 14th September at 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "School of Health Sciences and Social Work"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000145413044": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Level B) - Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "The School of Applied Psychology is a national leader in accredited psychology training, with award winning educators and a strong focus on real world clinical skills. Our research drives national and international practice, with strengths in health behaviour, child and family interventions, youth development, workplace wellbeing and cognition. We offer extensive industry partnerships and work integrated learning across all levels of study. As a Lecturer in Clinical Psychology , you will deliver high-quality teaching and clinical training within the School of Applied Psychology. You will support an outstanding, student-centred learning experience across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. As a Lecturer you will: Deliver engaging teaching across psychology, counselling, clinical psychology and professional psychology programs. Provide high quality clinical supervision to postgraduate students. Coordinate courses and contribute to associated academic administration. Improve teaching through evaluation, professional development and scholarly practice. Build positive relationships with students, colleagues, industry and community partners. This is a continuing, part-time (0.60FTE), position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. \n\n You are a qualified clinical psychologist committed to evidence-based practice, high quality teaching and the development of future psychology professionals. To be successful, you will have: A PhD or doctoral qualification in clinical psychology or a related field. Current AHPRA registration with an area of practice endorsement in clinical psychology. Eligibility to provide supervision under Psychology Board of Australia requirements. Demonstrated ability to deliver student centred teaching and effective clinical supervision. Strong interpersonal and collaborative skills, with a commitment to improving teaching practice. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Opportunities for internal mobility How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Allison Waters, Head of School - School of Applied Psychology at HoS-appliedpsychology@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, please contact Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at m.mahon@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 13th September 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "School of Applied Psychology"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000145383519": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Pharmacy ",
      "description": "The School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences is entering an exciting period of growth. With increasing student demand and a strong commitment to delivering an exceptional pharmacy education experience, we are expanding our Pharmacy team and seeking a Lecturer (Level B) who wants to help shape the next chapter of our success. This is an opportunity to join a collegial and forward-looking school that is preparing graduates for a rapidly evolving healthcare landscape. You'll work alongside passionate educators, researchers and clinicians who are committed to innovation, excellence and making a real difference to the health of communities. Whether your passion lies in pharmacy practice, pharmacotherapy, curriculum innovation, student learning or building stronger connections with the profession, this role offers the opportunity to contribute, influence and grow. You will bring your contemporary pharmacy expertise into the classroom, inspire future pharmacists, and help create learning experiences that connect education with real-world practice. As a Lecturer in Pharmacy, you will contribute to teaching across Pharmacy Practice, Pharmacotherapy and related areas, while also supporting curriculum development, professional engagement and student research opportunities. Key responsibilities include: Developing and delivering engaging teaching and assessment in Pharmacotherapy and/or Pharmacy Practice. Creating an outstanding student experience across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Contributing to course coordination, curriculum development and innovative approaches to learning. Supporting Honours and postgraduate pharmacy students through high-quality research experiences. Building industry and community partnerships and contributing to research that influences pharmacy education and practice. This is a part-time (0.8 FTE), continuing position based at Griffith University’s Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. \n\n To be successful in this role, you will hold a degree in Pharmacy and have substantial professional experience relevant to the discipline, including at least 5 years working within a clinical pharmacy environment. You will have: Current professional registration as a Pharmacist with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra). Demonstrated knowledge and experience in Pharmacotherapy and/or Pharmacy Practice. Experience teaching Pharmacotherapy and/or Pharmacy Practice in a higher education setting will be highly regarded. A commitment to student-centred learning and the ongoing development of pharmacy education. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: 50% fee discount for work related post graduate Griffith degrees  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the Position Description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Jennifer Boddy, Head of School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences at j.boddy@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner at j.dhall@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Tuesday, 22 September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences"
    },
