    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000142043849": {
      "title": "CSIRO Industry PhD Scholarship - Training Humanoid Robots for High-Risk Applications using Large and Small AI Models",
      "description": "We are currently looking for a PhD candidate to develop trustworthy artificial intelligence for humanoid robots operating in hazardous environments. The primary focus of this role is to integrate computer vision, large and small AI models, formal reasoning, reinforcement learning, and robot control so that humanoid robots can interpret mission goals, plan safe actions, and perform complex manipulation tasks. This CSIRO Industry PhD project includes hands-on research using robotic platforms, multimodal sensors, simulation environments, and industry-relevant scenarios in explosive ordnance disposal, mining, and construction. Success in this role requires close collaboration with researchers and engineers from Griffith University, CSIRO, and Cyborg Dynamics Engineering. This position is based primarily at Griffith University’s Brisbane South (Nathan) campus for three days per week, with the remaining two days spent at our industry partner, Cyborg Dynamics. As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. \n\n The selection of applicants for higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University considers academic merit and research experience. To succeed in this role, you will have a strong background in artificial intelligence, computer science, robotics, machine learning, or a related field, together with proficiency in Python and modern machine learning frameworks. You will demonstrate a passion for robotics and trustworthy AI, strong problem-solving and communication skills, and a desire to undertake industry-engaged research in computer vision, reinforcement learning, embodied intelligence, and autonomous systems. Expressions of interest are welcome from Australian or New Zealand citizens, or Australian permanent residents ONLY. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to  first-class honours , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Policy . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program, refer  here . Applicants should have an academic background in robotics and AI. \n\n About the scholarship \nThis scholarship offers a generous stipend of $48,071 per annum (indexed) for four years, based on the 2026 rate, plus additional funding for project expenses and professional development starting from $13,000 per year (indexed). What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EOI Process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  z.hou@griffith.edu.au , containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Brief research proposal, maximum 2 pages Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the ‘About you’ section A curriculum vitae (CV) Names and contact details of two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is:  Friday 25 September 2026 at 5pm AEST. The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line For project related enquiries please contact: \nDr Zhe Hou \nEmail:  z.hou@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nThe PhD Partnerships Team \nEmail:  PhDPartnerships@griffith.edu.au \n\n Griffith University’s School of Information and Communication Technology delivers industry-focused teaching and research across artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, data science, software engineering, robotics and digital technologies. Its researchers develop intelligent systems that address real-world challenges, supported by strong partnerships with industry, government and the wider community. The supervisors for this PhD Project will be Dr Zhe Hou and Dr Ernest Foo.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000142017299": {
      "error": "not present in bulk fetch result"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000141838334": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "The Griffith Centre for Mental Health is a leading research centre dedicated to improving mental health outcomes through evidence-based research, clinical innovation, and strong partnerships with health services and communities. This exciting opportunity sits within nationally significant research programs focused on improving access to effective treatments for children and young people experiencing obsessive compulsive disorder (OCD), including major projects funded by the Medical Research Future Fund (MRFF) and the National Health and Medical Research Council (NHMRC). We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow (Grade 1) to join the Centre for Mental Health and contribute to the delivery of two major nationally funded clinical research programs focused on child and adolescent OCD. The successful candidate will play a key role in supporting research delivery, project coordination, intervention and assessment activities, and the development of high-impact research outputs. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Contribute to the delivery of research objectives across the Centre's major mental health research projects. Coordinate research activities, assessments, and intervention delivery within clinical trials. Prepare publications, presentations, and research reports arising from project outcomes. Develop a strong publication record in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals and contribute to competitive grant applications. Assist in the supervision and mentoring of Honours and Higher Degree Research students. Supervise Research Assistants involved in trial activities. Ensure compliance with ethical, safety, and university policies and procedures. Champion professionalism, integrity, and collaboration in line with the University's values and Code of Conduct. This is a full time, fixed term position until August 2029 primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast campus. As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full time equivalent base salary will be Research Fellow Grade 1 range $91,705 - $107,420 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $107,295 - $125,682 per annum. \n\n What matters most is your drive to create a brighter future that benefits all. Through our core principles of excellence, ethics and engagement, you’ll thrive on seeing the direct and lasting impact you’ll have on every community and every future. You will also have: PhD in Psychology or an equivalent qualification and/or relevant professional experience. Demonstrated experience in child and adolescent mental health research and practice. Experience delivering evidence-based psychological assessments and interventions. Registration or Provisional Registration as a Psychologist with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Strong project management, organisational, and communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary research teams. Demonstrated commitment to research excellence and publication outcomes. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Lara Farrell, Director, Griffith Centre of Mental Health at l.farrell@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, please contact Maria Mahon, Talent Acquisition Partner at m.mahon@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Monday, 21 September at 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "Griffith Health"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000140590059": {
      "title": "First Peoples Employment Talent Network ",
      "description": "The First Peoples Employment Talent Network provides an opportunity to express your interest in working at Griffith and connect with future employment opportunities across our campuses in both professional and academic areas.  When you apply to join the network, your experience, skills and transferable capabilities will be reviewed to ensure they reflect Griffith's workforce needs. If your application aligns, our First Peoples Employment Partner will contact you to discuss your application.  As a member of the Talent Network, you will be notified of future opportunities that may arise across Griffith's campuses at Brisbane South (Nathan), Gold Coast, Logan and South Bank.  To be considered for this network, candidates should be an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   \n\n Why Join Griffith?  \nAt Griffith, we recognise that employment is about more than a job. It's about belonging, growth, connection and opportunity.  Our  First Peoples Employment Action Plan  is focused on creating the conditions for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees to flourish through cultural safety, leadership development, professional growth, meaningful career pathways and strong community connections. We are committed to ensuring First Peoples staff feel valued, respected and empowered to achieve their career aspirations.   When you join Griffith, you'll become part of a values-led organisation guided by excellence, inclusion, integrity, innovation and reciprocity.    We offer:  A culturally safe and inclusive workplace that values Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and cultures.  Opportunities to connect with other First Peoples staff through dedicated staff networks and community-building initiatives.   Leadership, learning and professional development opportunities designed to support career progression and long-term success.   Flexible work arrangements, including a mix of work-from-home and on-campus options.  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts.  Generous leave provisions, including paid First Peoples Cultural leave, paid parental leave and leave loading.  Support for future study and professional development through Griffith's Educational Staff Assistance Scheme.  Opportunities to contribute to Indigenous-led research, education and community engagement initiatives that create meaningful impact.   You may be an experienced professional, academic, researcher, recent graduate or someone looking to bring your transferable skills into the higher education sector. Through the First Peoples Employment Talent Network, Griffith seeks to build relationships with talented Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are interested in contributing to a university that values Indigenous leadership, knowledge and excellence.   Griffith University values equity, diversity and inclusion. For more information, please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. If you require any accessibility adjustments to submit your application, please contact us. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  \n \n How to apply  \nPlease submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following:  Current curriculum vitae, including name and contact details.  Cover Letter which should be no more than 2 pages in length.  The First Peoples Employment Talent Network is only open to Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander applicants - people who:   a) are of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent; and   \nb) identify as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person; and   \nc) are accepted by their community as being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   Further Information  \nFor further information about the First Peoples Talent Network visit  griffith.edu.au/equity/first-peoples-employment  or contact Bronwyn Horn, First Peoples Employment Partner at  b.horn@griffith.edu.au . You can also stay up to date with all recruitment activity at Griffith via our  First Peoples Employment at Griffith LinkedIn  group.   \n\n Join Griffith University and be part of a community where Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are supported to flourish.  At Griffith, we are committed to creating the conditions for First Peoples staff to thrive. We aspire to be the university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples by fostering a culturally safe workplace, supporting career growth and leadership, celebrating Indigenous knowledges, and creating meaningful employment opportunities across the University.",
      "department": "Corporate Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000140589949": {
      "title": "First Peoples Employment Talent Network",
      "description": "The First Peoples Employment Talent Network provides an opportunity to express your interest in working at Griffith and connect with future employment opportunities across our campuses in both professional and academic areas.  When you apply to join the network, your experience, skills and transferable capabilities will be reviewed to ensure they reflect Griffith's workforce needs. If your application aligns, our First Peoples Employment Partner will contact you to discuss your application.  As a member of the Talent Network, you will be notified of future opportunities that may arise across Griffith's campuses at Brisbane South (Nathan), Gold Coast, Logan and South Bank.  To be considered for this network, candidates should be an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   \n\n Why Join Griffith?  \nAt Griffith, we recognise that employment is about more than a job. It's about belonging, growth, connection and opportunity.  Our  First Peoples Employment Action Plan  is focused on creating the conditions for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees to flourish through cultural safety, leadership development, professional growth, meaningful career pathways and strong community connections. We are committed to ensuring First Peoples staff feel valued, respected and empowered to achieve their career aspirations.   When you join Griffith, you'll become part of a values-led organisation guided by excellence, inclusion, integrity, innovation and reciprocity.    We offer:  A culturally safe and inclusive workplace that values Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and cultures.  Opportunities to connect with other First Peoples staff through dedicated staff networks and community-building initiatives.   Leadership, learning and professional development opportunities designed to support career progression and long-term success.   Flexible work arrangements, including a mix of work-from-home and on-campus options.  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts.  Generous leave provisions, including paid First Peoples Cultural leave, paid parental leave and leave loading.  Support for future study and professional development through Griffith's Educational Staff Assistance Scheme.  Opportunities to contribute to Indigenous-led research, education and community engagement initiatives that create meaningful impact.   You may be an experienced professional, academic, researcher, recent graduate or someone looking to bring your transferable skills into the higher education sector. Through the First Peoples Employment Talent Network, Griffith seeks to build relationships with talented Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are interested in contributing to a university that values Indigenous leadership, knowledge and excellence.   Griffith University values equity, diversity and inclusion. For more information, please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. If you require any accessibility adjustments to submit your application, please contact us. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  \n \n How to apply  \nPlease submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following:  Current curriculum vitae, including name and contact details.  Cover Letter which should be no more than 2 pages in length.  The First Peoples Employment Talent Network is only open to Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander applicants - people who:   a) are of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent; and   \nb) identify as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person; and   \nc) are accepted by their community as being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   Further Information  \nFor further information about the First Peoples Talent Network visit  griffith.edu.au/equity/first-peoples-employment  or contact Bronwyn Horn, First Peoples Employment Partner at  b.horn@griffith.edu.au . You can also stay up to date with all recruitment activity at Griffith via our  First Peoples Employment at Griffith LinkedIn  group.   \n\n Join Griffith University and be part of a community where Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are supported to flourish.  At Griffith, we are committed to creating the conditions for First Peoples staff to thrive. We aspire to be the university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples by fostering a culturally safe workplace, supporting career growth and leadership, celebrating Indigenous knowledges, and creating meaningful employment opportunities across the University.",
      "department": "Corporate Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000140111718": {
      "title": "First Peoples Employment Talent Network",
      "description": "The First Peoples Employment Talent Network provides an opportunity to express your interest in working at Griffith and connect with future employment opportunities across our campuses in both professional and academic areas.  When you apply to join the network, your experience, skills and transferable capabilities will be reviewed to ensure they reflect Griffith's workforce needs. If your application aligns, our First Peoples Employment Partner will contact you to discuss your application.  As a member of the Talent Network, you will be notified of future opportunities that may arise across Griffith's campuses at Brisbane South (Nathan), Gold Coast, Logan and South Bank.  To be considered for this network, candidates should be an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   \n\n Why Join Griffith?  \nAt Griffith, we recognise that employment is about more than a job. It's about belonging, growth, connection and opportunity.  Our  First Peoples Employment Action Plan  is focused on creating the conditions for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees to flourish through cultural safety, leadership development, professional growth, meaningful career pathways and strong community connections. We are committed to ensuring First Peoples staff feel valued, respected and empowered to achieve their career aspirations.   When you join Griffith, you'll become part of a values-led organisation guided by excellence, inclusion, integrity, innovation and reciprocity.    We offer:  A culturally safe and inclusive workplace that values Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and cultures.  Opportunities to connect with other First Peoples staff through dedicated staff networks and community-building initiatives.   Leadership, learning and professional development opportunities designed to support career progression and long-term success.   Flexible work arrangements, including a mix of work-from-home and on-campus options.  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts.  Generous leave provisions, including paid First Peoples Cultural leave, paid parental leave and leave loading.  Support for future study and professional development through Griffith's Educational Staff Assistance Scheme.  Opportunities to contribute to Indigenous-led research, education and community engagement initiatives that create meaningful impact.   You may be an experienced professional, academic, researcher, recent graduate or someone looking to bring your transferable skills into the higher education sector. Through the First Peoples Employment Talent Network, Griffith seeks to build relationships with talented Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are interested in contributing to a university that values Indigenous leadership, knowledge and excellence.   Griffith University values equity, diversity and inclusion. For more information, please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. If you require any accessibility adjustments to submit your application, please contact us. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  \n \n How to apply  \nPlease submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following:  Current curriculum vitae, including name and contact details.  Cover Letter which should be no more than 2 pages in length.  The First Peoples Employment Talent Network is only open to Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander applicants - people who:   a) are of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent; and   \nb) identify as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person; and   \nc) are accepted by their community as being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   Further Information  \nFor further information about the First Peoples Talent Network visit  griffith.edu.au/equity/first-peoples-employment  or contact Bronwyn Horn, First Peoples Employment Partner at  b.horn@griffith.edu.au . You can also stay up to date with all recruitment activity at Griffith via our  First Peoples Employment at Griffith LinkedIn  group.   \n\n Join Griffith University and be part of a community where Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are supported to flourish.  At Griffith, we are committed to creating the conditions for First Peoples staff to thrive. We aspire to be the university of choice for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples by fostering a culturally safe workplace, supporting career growth and leadership, celebrating Indigenous knowledges, and creating meaningful employment opportunities across the University.",
      "department": "Corporate Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000120831317": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarships: Machine Vision",
      "description": "This research aims to advance knowledge of machine vision for deep visual understanding of natural objects and environments. The primary focus of this role is to undertake fundamental research in visual understanding and multimodal machine learning. Research activities include developing novel deep learning methods for representation learning, vision-language reasoning, fine-grained and ultra-fine-grained visual categorization, and trustworthy AI systems. The candidate will publish high-quality research papers in leading conferences and journals in computer vision and machine learning. Successful candidates will have the opportunity to receive advanced research training and work within a vibrant research environment that includes a team of research fellows, industry collaborators, and PhD students. The position provides opportunities for collaboration with leading researchers and participation in international research communities in computer vision, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of academic merit and research background. To be successful in this role, you should demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving skills, solid mathematical foundation, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a research environment. Evidence of a passion for computer vision and image processing is essential. Previous experiences in deep learning, visual recognition, multimodal AI, pattern recognition, or data-driven modelling are preferred. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to  first-class honours , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Policy . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program, refer  here . Please note : Applicants with academic qualifications in computer science, engineering, applied mathematics, with a publication record in top tier venues such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, AAAI, IJCAI are preferred. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 OR A score of no less than 3+ in each skill of the ISLPR (conducted by ISLPR Language Services only) OR A minimum overall score of 176 (no score less than 169) on C1 Advanced  or  C2 Proficiency OR An overall score of 58 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 50 (applies to tests taken prior to 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 55 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 47 (applies to tests taken on or after 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 70 in the LanguageCert Academic OR An overall score of 59 in the Michigan English Test (MET) . \n\n About the scholarship \nThe successful candidate will be awarded a Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship (GUPRS) or an equivalent scholarship package funded through the ARC Industry Laureate Fellowship. \n \nThe 2026 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $35,656 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the GUPRS Conditions of Award for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the GUIPRS Conditions of Award for more information. \n \n EoI process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to yongsheng.gao@griffith.edu.au, containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Brief research proposal, maximum 2 pages Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the ‘About you’ section A curriculum vitae (CV) Names and contact details of two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is: Currently Open  The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line \n \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). \n \n Further information For project related enquiries please contact: \nProfessor Yongsheng Gao \nEmail:  yongsheng.gao@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n We are currently looking for 4 highly motivated PhD candidates to join the research of “Next-Generation Visual Understanding” funded by the ARC Industry Laureate Fellowship. The successful candidate will join the research team led by an Australian Industry Laureate Fellow and internationally recognized researchers in smart farming, computer vision, machine learning, and artificial intelligence, within the School of Engineering and Built Environment at Griffith University. The research environment is collaborative and multidisciplinary, combining expertise in deep learning, computer vision, data science, and applied AI, and working closely with industry partners, national research institutions, and international collaborators. \n \nThis opportunity will be primarily based at the Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000071420565": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarship:  Validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis",
      "description": "We are currently seeking highly motivated PhD candidates to join our research team at Griffith University. This exciting project aims to develop and validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis. Highlights of working on this project include: Focus on non-invasive, saliva-based diagnostics for liver fibrosis. Integration of clinical collaboration with hospital partners and cutting-edge research in the laboratory. Opportunity to work at the intersection of translational medicine, proteomics, and biomarker development. \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful in this role, you should have: A strong academic background in Medical Laboratory Science, Pathology, Molecular Pathology, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research experience working at the interface with hospital laboratories and working with clinicians. Evidence of collaborative skills and the ability to work effectively with clinical and laboratory-based research teams. A clear passion for research and a commitment to advancing the field of liver fibrosis paving the way for precision health. Should hold a valid Australian driver's licence. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed, or expect to complete, a bachelors degree with honours equivalent to  first  class honours or a Masters degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a bachelor honours degree or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Procedure .  For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program refer  here . Please note : Applicants must have obtained a Master’s degree or an Honours degree in relative fields. A solid background in Medical Laboratory Science, Pathology, Molecular Pathology with an interest in biomarker discovery is required. Some experience in the field of multivariate statistical analysis would be beneficial but is not required. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A minimum score of 575 on the paper-based TOEFL including a score of no less than 5.0 on the TWE OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 \n\n About the scholarship \nThe 2025 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $34,752 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the  GUPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the  GUIPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EoI process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  c.punyadeera@griffith.edu.au  containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section, including a  copy of your academic transcript A curriculum vitae (CV) using the  Griffith CV template . Names of  two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is:  Tuesday 29 July 2025 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line For project related enquiries please contact: \nProfessor Chamindie Punyadeera \nEmail: c.punyadeera@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n The Saliva and Liquid Biopsy Group is dedicated to advancing biomarker discovery for metabolic diseases and cancer, with the goal of improving precision health. Our research focuses on identifying and validating biomarkers that enable more accurate patient stratification based on disease risk, prognosis, and treatment response. The successful PhD applicant will be based at the Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics (IBG), Griffith University, Brisbane South (Nathan) and will work within a collaborative and interdisciplinary environment. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000040674965": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarship:  Synthetic biopolymer-protein conjugates for enhanced mucosal delivery of drugs and antigens",
      "description": "We are currently looking for a PhD candidate to develop innovative biopolymer-protein conjugates for enhanced mucosal delivery of drugs and antigens. This will include electrohydrodynamic atomisation for nasal delivery. The primary focus of this role is to design and develop functional biopolymers that target the mucosa and that are amendable toward electrohydrodynamic atomisation to overcome the current drug and antigen delivery limitations. The project aims to enhance the efficacy of biopolymer micro/nanoparticles through precise control of particle size and charge and fill the gap between the fast advancement in nasal drug and vaccine discovery and conventional ineffective delivery techniques. Success in this role requires knowledge in design of functional polymer particles, generation of cell factories as production strains, bioprocess development and characterisation of nanomaterials before and after the nebulising process. \n  \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful within this role, you will be able to work in bioengineering, microfluidics, and material science. You will have evidence of a passion for conducting high impact research, with strong desire to undertake research in multidisciplinary research. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed, or expect to complete, a bachelors degree with honours equivalent to  first  class honours or a Masters degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a bachelor honours degree or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Procedure .  For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program refer  here . Please note : You should have strong background in Material/Biomaterial science and experiences in design, analysis, fabrication and characterization of new material samples. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A minimum score of 575 on the paper-based TOEFL including a score of no less than 5.0 on the TWE OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 \n  \n\n About the scholarship \nThe 2025 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $34,752 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the  GUPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the  GUIPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. \n \n EoI process \nPlease do not  select the “I'm Interested” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  v.dau@griffith.edu.au  containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section, including a  copy of your academic transcript A curriculum vitae (CV) using the  Griffith CV template . Names of two referees Closing date of expressions of interest: Friday 7 March 2025 at 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship online. \n \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across locations in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). \n \n Further information For project related enquiries please contact: \nDr Van Dau \nEmail:  v.dau@griffith.edu.au \n \nProfessor Bernd Rehm \nEmail:  b.rehm@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n Working for one of the most influential universities in Australia and the Asia–Pacific region, you will join a University that spans five physical locations in South East Queensland and all disciplines, while our network of more than 200,000 graduates extends worldwide. We have world-class facilities for micro- and nanotechnology and advanced manufacturing. You will conduct the advanced research at the Centre for Cell Factories and Biopolymers, the centre equipped with modern bioprocessing equipment, including cell disruptors, homogenisers, bioreactors, and chromatography system. It is also located in a PC2 laboratory which is equipped with an array of instruments that enable synthetic biology of bacterial production strain. This opportunity will be primarily based at Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000149239319": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant",
      "description": "Griffith University Dental Assistant | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Dental Assistant Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Off Campus Location Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: GHC - Learning and Teaching - CLT Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Griffith Health Clinics provide high-quality primary healthcare services while supporting the education and training of the next generation of health professionals. Based at Warwick, we are seeking a Dental Assistant to support students and staff in delivering exceptional patient care. Key responsibilities for this role will include: Assist staff and students across a broad range of dental treatments and procedures. Prepare patients for treatment and support clinic operations, working autonomously and using initiative to manage day-to-day responsibilities effectively. Maintain clinical hygiene and adhere to infection control protocols. Provide administrative and reception support. Uphold university values and comply with policies, health and safety requirements, and professional About you To be successful in this role, you will hold: An Australian Dental Assistant qualification or recognised equivalent is highly desirable. Current CPR/First Aid Certification from a recognised provider. Current Queensland Blue Card (or willingness to obtain). In addition to the above, you will demonstrate: Excellent teamwork and communication skills. Ability to work under supervision and contribute to efficient clinic operations. Strong administrative skills with attention to detail. A commitment to patient care and student learning. What we can offer This is a full-time, fixed-term position until October 2027, based primarily at Griffith University’s Warwick location. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 4 range $76,126 - $80,321 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $89,067 - $93,976 per annum. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact the Dental Clinic Manager at [email protected] . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] . Closing date: Wednesday, 30 September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000149237749": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "Griffith University Research Fellow | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Research Fellow Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences - PAM Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description The School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences is a leading centre for health research and education at Griffith University, bringing together researchers, clinicians and industry partners to advance discoveries that improve health outcomes locally and globally. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to join the Artificial Heart Frontiers Program (AHFP) funded by the Medical Research Future Fund (MRFF). The successful candidate will work within the Biorheology Research Laboratory at the Gold Coast campus of Griffith University and contribute to the delivery of this multidisciplined research project. The AHFP is a multi-institution partnership between academia and industry, has secured investment from the MRFF to develop artificial hearts and related technologies. We have teamed with leading academic, healthcare and industry partners to launch a new program to develop the world’s most advanced artificial heart, and the next generation of cardiovascular technology to support all patients with heart failure. Griffith University’s involvement is led by the Director of the Biorheology Research Laboratory, Professor Michael Simmonds, who is the Haemocompatibility Lead and serves the Executive Committee of the AHFP. Supported through a $50 million MRFF grant, the AHFP is expanding its research and commercialisation activities to help shape the future of heart failure treatment through innovative cardiovascular technologies. This is a full time, fixed term position until June 2028 primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The successful candidate will be appointed at either Research Fellow Grade 1 or Research Fellow Grade 2 , depending on their qualifications, skills, experience and demonstrated level of research expertise. The full-time equivalent base salary will be at Research Fellow Grade 1 range $91,705 - $107,420 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $107,295 - $125,682 per annum. The full-time equivalent base salary will be at Research Fellow Grade 2 range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. Qualifications To be successful in this role, you will hold a PhD or equivalent qualifications/work experience in blood rheology, or a similar field. You will have: Experience working in the field of Biomedical and/or Haemocompatibility research and reporting on research findings. Experience in working with ASTM standards such as F1841, F1830-97, F2888 and F2382. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the Position Description: Research Fellow Grade 1 / Research Fellow Grade 2 Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Michael Simmonds, Head of School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences at [email protected] . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] . Closing date: Monday, 5 October 2026 at 11:59 pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000149232849": {
      "title": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia",
      "description": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia Full-time Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: DVC Research - SDV Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description We are currently looking for a PhD candidate to undertake research on anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia, which is a growing national security concern. The primary focus of the PhD project is to develop new knowledge about the drivers of these forms of extremism and to work with the research team and industry partners to evaluate interventions that might mitigate the risk of violence against public officials. This project includes the possibility of working with a mix of survey, observation, interviews, and/or social media data. Success in this role requires collaboration with the supervisory team and industry partners associated with the project. This PhD project is embedded within a broader research project on anti-government extremism funded by the Office of National Intelligence Discovery Grant Scheme.  It is expected that  the preferred applicant will be available to commence in early 2027. This position will be based at either the Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast campus. As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Job Description The research will be undertaken within the School of Criminology & Criminal Justice at Griffith University.  Griffith University was recently ranked #1 in Australia for its research on peace, justice and strong institutions and #2 in the world for Impact (2026 Times Higher Education Impact Ratings).  You will work specifically within Griffith University’s School of Criminology & Criminal Justice community, the largest in Australia, and widely considered Australia’s #1 criminology research program. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility. Qualifications The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful within this role, you will be able to demonstrate strong analytical skills, have demonstrated experience using the research methods described above, and be able to work independently as part of a research team. You must be able to communicate research findings clearly in writing and in presentations, and engage critically with current literature on procedural justice as well as radicalisation and extremism. You will have evidence of a passion for extremism-related research and have a strong desire to undertake research on anti-government and Sovereign citizen forms of extremism. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic applicants only.  As the project has been funded by the Office of National Intelligence applicants are required to be Australian citizens, Australian permanent residents, or New Zealand special category Visa holders. Note that proof of your status must be provided and approved by the Office of National Intelligence before an offer of scholarship is made. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to first-class honours or second-class honours (Division A) , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the HDR Scholarship Policy . a record of research, or a qualification granted by a professional or other body deemed by the Dean, Griffith Graduate Research School, to be of a comparable standard.  For further information please refer to the Equivalent Qualifications for HDR Program Admission web page. Please note : Applicants with a background in psychology, criminology, political science or a cognate discipline are being sought, with additional experience working in the national intelligence or policing field being a distinct advantage. Additional Information About the scholarship The 2026 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $35,656 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the GUPRS Conditions of Award for more information. The successful applicant will also be awarded a scholarship top-up of $20,000 per annum for three years from the Office of National Intelligence funded project. The total annual stipend for 3 years will be $55,656. The candidate will also be eligible to access a further $4,500 from the School of Criminology & Criminal Justice to support their research, to undertake relevant professional development, or to attend conferences to present their research. What Griffith offers As a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EOI Process Please do not select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to Professor Kristina Murphy ( t.murphy@griffith.edu.au ), containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship and why you are interested in joining the research project. Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section (e.g., academic transcript), with a brief discussion of the research component of this program. A curriculum vitae (CV)  with your contact details using the Griffith CV template . Names and contact details of two referees  who can comment about your suitability to undertake study at a PhD level. Evidence of Australian citizenship, permanent residency, or New Zealand special category Visa holder. The closing date for expressions of interest is: Friday the 16th of October 2026 The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line. For project related enquiries please contact: Professor Kristina Murphy (Tina) Email: t.murphy@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: Griffith Graduate Research School Email: hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Foundation Models for Anomaly Detection Nathan, Australia Senior Commercial Research Officer Southport, Australia Senior Commercial Research Officer Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148923906": {
      "title": "Griffith University Consultant Opportunity: Regional Marketing Manager (Greater China)",
      "description": "Griffith University Consultant Opportunity: Regional Marketing Manager (Greater China) | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Consultant Opportunity: Regional Marketing Manager (Greater China) Full-time Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Griffith International - GDR Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description At Griffith, we believe excellence should always be purposeful. Established to challenge convention, we are proud to be a university driven by the impact we make. From leading-edge research to empowering students from across the globe, our work is grounded in the belief that education and knowledge should always serve a greater good. Job Description Griffith University is seeking to engage a locally based consultant to undertake marketing and agent support activities for the recruitment of international students. This is a great opportunity for a high performing individual to work with the dynamic Griffith International team and make an impact in the lives of future Griffith University students. Griffith University has a long and highly valued relationship with Greater China, through research and collaboration, and an ever-growing network of alumni. With a locally based representative, Griffith International will provide increased support to its education agents and strategic partners, enhance the standing of the University’s profile, and assist with the recruitment of students and provision of international student support. This is a full-time, one-year contract position based in either Shanghai, East China region or Beijing, and will require regular travel China when required. Travel to Australia may also be required occasionally. The role The consultant is responsible for the development and implementation of marketing plans and initiatives to support the recruitment of international students from China. The consultant will work closely with the Regional Director (Greater China and Mongolia), to support and manage the University’s agent network, and strategic partners and stakeholders, in effectively counselling and supporting new students in their decision and plans to undertake study at Griffith University. About You You are an experienced international marketing professional with a deep understanding of the education sector, especially within China. You thrive in cross-cultural settings and can independently manage a complex workload under broad direction. To succeed, you will have: A relevant tertiary qualification and demonstrated experience in international education marketing and student recruitment. Fluency in English and Mandarin. Demonstrated success in achieving student recruitment, conversion and enrolment outcomes, preferably within the international education sector. Proven ability to identify recruitment opportunities and develop effective marketing strategies. Proven ability to develop and maintain productive relationships with education agents, institutional partners and other stakeholders. In-depth knowledge of the Australian higher education landscape and compliance frameworks. Strong interpersonal, communication, and negotiation skills. A valid work permit for China or the ability to obtain one. Ability and willingness to undertake regular domestic and international travel. What We Offer A competitive remuneration package will be negotiated on a fee for service basis with the successful consultant. This is not an expatriate package position. Additional information For additional information about this opportunity download the state of purpose. Enquiries should be directed to Ms Jennifer Zhang, Regional Director (Greater China and Mongolia), via email at jennifer.zhang@griffith.edu.au or phone +86 18601272579. Closing date : Wednesday 30th September 2026 at 5:00 pm (AEST). All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Dental Assistant Warwick, Australia Research Fellow Southport, Australia Cyber Security Improvement Program Manager Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Consultant Opportunity: Regional Marketing Manager (Greater China) Shanghai, East China region or Beijing,, Beijing, China Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148918619": {
      "title": "Griffith University Cyber Security Improvement Program Manager",
      "description": "Griffith University Cyber Security Improvement Program Manager | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Cyber Security Improvement Program Manager Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Cyber Security EIC - CYB Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the Opportunity The Cyber Security Improvement Program Manager provides strategic leadership and oversight for Griffith University's Cyber Security Improvement Program (CSIP), a complex, university-wide transformation initiative aimed at strengthening cyber resilience and security capabilities. Accountable for the end-to-end management of the program, the role directs planning, reporting, financial and resource management, governance, risk and issue management, assurance, stakeholder engagement, organisational change, and benefits realisation across multiple projects and workstreams. Reporting to the Director, Cyber Security, the position leads program teams and serves as a key advisor to executive leadership and governance committees, ensuring the successful delivery of sustainable and measurable program outcomes. Key Responsibilities Lead and oversee the delivery of the Cyber Security Improvement Program (CSIP), ensuring alignment with strategic objectives and governance requirements. Provide regular reporting, advice and recommendations to executive leaders, sponsors and governance committees. Develop and maintain integrated program plans, roadmaps, milestones, resource requirements and delivery schedules. Manage program delivery to ensure scope, budget, timelines, quality standards and outcomes are achieved. Oversee the CSIP budget, including forecasting, expenditure monitoring, financial reporting and investment prioritisation. Manage supplier, contract and procurement activities in partnership with internal stakeholders and in accordance with University requirements. Establish and track program benefits, ensuring measurable improvements in cyber security capability, resilience, maturity and compliance. Lead program-level risk, issue, dependency and decision management, ensuring timely resolution and escalation where required. Coordinate assurance activities, audits and reviews, and oversee the implementation of resulting actions and recommendations. Build and maintain effective relationships with executive stakeholders, business leaders, technical teams and delivery partners. Lead stakeholder engagement and organisational change initiatives to support the successful adoption of new capabilities and ways of working. Provide leadership, coaching and performance management for program staff and assigned resources. Promote continuous improvement through lessons learned, best-practice program management and delivery excellence. Monitor emerging cyber security trends, risks and industry developments to inform program priorities and investment decisions. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant qualifications in program or project management, information technology, cyber security, business administration or a related discipline, together with relevant experience delivering cyber security projects or programs; Experience delivering projects using PRINCE2 methodologies Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and may be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 4 years primarily based at our Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 10 Salary – Base - $147,057.74 + 17% superannuation. Full package is $172,057.55. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 20th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Project Coordinator (Cyber Security) Nathan, Australia Facilities Manager South Brisbane, Australia Dental Assistant Warwick, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Cyber Security Improvement Program Manager 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148884049": {
      "title": "Griffith University Senior Content Producer",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Content Producer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Senior Content Producer Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Marketing and Communications - OER Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the Opportunity We're looking for a strategic content professional who combines exceptional writing skills with audience insight, content optimisation and stakeholder influence. As a Senior Content Producer, you'll be part of a team of copywriters, designers and videographers working across Griffith University's marketing, brand and student recruitment activities, creating content that connects with diverse audiences and supports strategic objectives. Working closely with our CX, product and student recruitment teams you'll craft content from concept through to delivery to bring our story to life across a broad range of owned channels, including websites, publications and emails. This is a hands-on role where you'll write, edit and refine content while balancing multiple projects and stakeholders. You'll translate complex information into clear, engaging narratives, champion content quality and consistency, and ensure content is accessible, audience-focused and effective. Beyond content creation, you'll contribute to content strategy, champion best-practice writing standards and help shape the use of emerging technologies, including approved AI tools, to improve content efficiency, and optimise how copy is developed, adapted and delivered across channels and audiences. If you're a strong writer with a strategic mindset and enjoy turning complex briefs into clear, engaging content, this role offers the opportunity to help shape how Griffith creates and delivers content in a rapidly evolving marketing landscape. About you Relevant tertiary qualifications in Journalism or Communications with a minimum of at least four years subsequent relevant work experience, or equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and may be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time, continuing opportunity primarily based at our Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 7 – Base range - $104,504.60 - $113,219.43 + 17% superannuation. Ful package - $122,270.38 - $132,466.72. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acqusition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Monday 28th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Dental Assistant Warwick, Australia Research Fellow Southport, Australia PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. × Continue Senior Content Producer 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148668599": {
      "title": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Foundation Models for Anomaly Detection",
      "description": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Foundation Models for Anomaly Detection | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . PhD Scholarship: Foundation Models for Anomaly Detection Full-time Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: DVC Research - SDV Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description We are currently looking for a PhD candidate to undertake research in anomaly detection and graph machine learning. The primary focus of this role is to develop foundation models and frameworks for detecting anomalous patterns across diverse graph datasets and application domains. This project includes investigating unified and transferable graph anomaly detection models, developing advanced graph representation learning and anomaly detection techniques. Success in this role requires collaboration with [the supervisory team and researchers in graph machine learning, anomaly detection, and trustworthy artificial intelligence. This position is primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Job Description This scholarship will be based within the School of Information and Communication Technology (ICT) at Griffith University. The successful candidate will join an active research environment in artificial intelligence and machine learning, with opportunities to work alongside researchers in graph machine learning, anomaly detection, trustworthy AI, and related areas. The project will be supervised by Dr Yixin Liu, ARC DECRA Fellow and Lecturer in the School of ICT. His research spans graph anomaly detection, generalizable and out-of-distribution graph learning, graph representation learning, and trustworthy artificial intelligence. Qualifications The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful within this role, you will be able to demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving skills, the capacity to undertake independent research, and effective written and verbal communication skills. You will have evidence of a passion for artificial intelligence and machine learning, with a strong desire to undertake research in graph machine learning and anomaly detection. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed, or expect to complete, a bachelors degree with honours equivalent to first class honours or a Masters degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a bachelor honours degree or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with the Equivalent qualifications for HDR program admission . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program refer here . Please note : Applicants are advised that the following backgrounds and skills are highly desirable: A strong academic background in computer science, artificial intelligence, machine learning, data science, or a closely related discipline. Experience with machine learning or deep learning, preferably including graph neural networks, graph representation learning, anomaly detection, or related topics. Programming experience in Python and familiarity with modern deep-learning frameworks such as PyTorch. Strong mathematical, analytical, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to design and conduct independent research. Evidence of research experience, publications, competitive scholarships, academic awards, or other indicators of research potential is desirable but not essential. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A minimum score of 575 on the paper-based TOEFL including a score of no less than 5.0 on the TWE OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19. Additional Information About the scholarship The 2026 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $35,656 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the GUPRS Conditions of Award for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years full time study. Please see the GUIPRS Conditions of Award for more information. What Griffith offers As a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). Through this project, you will be supported to develop advanced research capability in graph machine learning and anomaly detection, including designing new learning frameworks, conducting large-scale empirical studies, and communicating research outcomes through high-quality publications and conference presentations. You will work in a research environment with strong expertise in graph anomaly detection and generalizable graph learning, and will have opportunities to collaborate with researchers at Griffith University and external research partners. EOI Process Please do not select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to Dr Yixin Liu at yixin.liu@griffith.edu.au , containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section A curriculum vitae (CV) using the Griffith CV template Names of two referees. The closing date for expressions of interest is: Friday 25 September 2026 at 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line. For project related enquiries please contact: Dr Yixin Liu Email: yixin.liu@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: Griffith Graduate Research School Email: hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia Nathan, Australia Senior Commercial Research Officer Southport, Australia Senior Commercial Research Officer Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. PhD Scholarship: Foundation Models for Anomaly Detection Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148618750": {
      "title": "Griffith University Service Centre Support Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Service Centre Support Officer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Service Centre Support Officer Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Corporate Services Service Centre - SER Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The Service Centre. A team you’ll want to be a part of. When you join the Corporate Services Service Centre, you’ll be part of a team that delivers impact by enhancing digital experiences for the graduates of tomorrow, researchers of today and all those working to make it a brighter future. But we know it’s not just what you do that matters, it’s who you do it with. Our people will tell you – our team sets us apart. We promise a supportive and friendly environment where you’ll collaborate to make an impact. Job Description About the opportunity The newly established Service Centre delivers core University services and support to staff and students through easy to access channels to deliver a high quality service experience. The Service Centre aims to engage, enable and empower our customers through the provision of information and problem resolution services across key services or connect them to our specialised Corporate Services teams. The Service Centre Support Officer provides first-line support for staff and students seeking information and assistance on a range of core services such as employment, financial transactions and payments, travel, parking, facilities and IT. This position manages a high-volume of routine enquiries, processes and basic requests and is support by extensive knowledge articles, university policy and procedures to ensure advice and wayfinding is accurate and timely. This position will undergo an extensive and progressive training program to build up knowledge and experience in a range of services and to enable the effective use of our technology platforms. Key Responsibilities Act as the first point of contact for support for CS services, receiving and responding to enquires across multiple channels (Phone, Chat, Digital, In-person) in a timely and professional manner Provide professional frontline customer service, ensuring user enquires are handled with empathy and clarity, logged accurately, and resolved or escalated promptly to maintain a positive staff and student experience Maintain accurate records of user requests, cases, incidents, and resolutions in the service management system Contribute to continuous improvement by proactively identifying opportunities to make processes more efficient and effective. Contribute to the capture of knowledge in the Service Management tool, working in partnership with subject matter experts to ensure the ongoing accuracy and quality of information Ensure compliance with relevant legislation and University policies and procedures, including equity and health and safety and exhibit good practice in relation to same. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant qualifications or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. The successful candidate will show proven proficiency and experience in excellent customer service. You will be passionate about positive client outcomes and have qualifications to help support this. IT skills will be a must as well as an ability to navigate digital systems and orient clients within our educational infrastructure. What we can offer This is a full time, continuing opportunity based at the Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 4 – Base range - $76,126.29 - $80,321.54 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $89,067.75 - $93,976.19. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Thursday 24th September @ 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Research Support Officer Nathan, Australia Research Support Officer Southport, Australia Operations Coordinator (Open Space) Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Service Centre Support Officer 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148411515": {
      "title": "Griffith University Research Support Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Research Support Officer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Research Support Officer Full-time Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Education and Professional Studies - EDN Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Griffith University is seeking a dynamic and strategically minded Research Support Officer to play a pivotal role in advancing research excellence across the School of Education and Professional Studies and the Griffith Institute for Educational Research (GIER). Working closely with the Head and Dean, Education and Professional Studies, research leaders and key stakeholders, you will drive initiatives that strengthen research performance, foster a vibrant research culture, and build research capacity across the School and Institute. This influential role offers the opportunity to lead research development projects, support the growth of collaborative research groups and strategic partnerships, and enhance the visibility, impact and engagement of world-class research. If you are passionate about enabling research success, translating strategy into action, and supporting researchers to maximise their impact, this is an exciting opportunity to contribute to transformative research initiatives that make a difference in education and society. Key responsibilities include but not limited to: Lead research development initiatives by coordinating research groups, capacity-building programs and strategic projects that strengthen research performance and culture across the School and GIER. Provide expert research support and advice to senior leaders, researchers and committees on research priorities, opportunities, governance and strategic initiatives. Drive research funding success through the coordination of grant development activities, funding opportunities and collaborative research partnerships. Enhance research visibility and impact by implementing communication, engagement and knowledge translation activities that promote the profile and influence of School and GIER research. Deliver research performance insights and governance support through data analysis, reporting, stakeholder engagement and the coordination of research planning and decision-making processes. About you The successful candidate will have a relevant postgraduate qualification and/or substantial experience in research development, research management, higher education administration or a related field. You will also have: Demonstrated experience leading and coordinating research development initiatives, strategic projects, research groups or capacity-building programs, with the ability to deliver outcomes in complex organisational environments. Proven ability to support research funding activities, facilitate collaboration, and build productive relationships with researchers, industry, government, community and other external stakeholders. Highly developed written and verbal communication skills, with experience developing and implementing strategies that enhance research visibility, engagement, reputation and impact across diverse audiences. Demonstrated ability to analyse complex data and information, prepare high-quality reports and briefing materials, and provide evidence-based advice to support strategic planning, governance and decision-making. Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to work collaboratively, influence outcomes and build effective partnerships across a broad range of stakeholders. Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, coordinate multiple initiatives, and identify opportunities for process and service improvement. Desirable: Experience working within a university, research institute or knowledge-intensive environment. Knowledge of the Australian higher education and research funding landscape, including competitive grant schemes, research impact and engagement frameworks. What we can offer This is a fixed term (available until 31 December 2026), full-time position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast (preferred) or Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time base salary for a HEW Level 7 is in the range $104,504 - $113,219 per annum, plus 17% employer superannuation. The total FTE package is in the range $122,270 - $132,466 per annum. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About you section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights.  Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Debbie Heck, Head and Dean, School of Education and Professional Studies at d.heck@griffith.edu.au . For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Theresa Burke, Talent Acquisition Partner on t.burke@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Tuesday, 15 September 2026 at 11.59pm. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Research Fellow Southport, Australia PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia Nathan, Australia Consultant Opportunity: Regional Marketing Manager (Greater China) Beijing, China Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Research Support Officer 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148411539": {
      "title": "Griffith University Research Support Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Research Support Officer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Research Support Officer Full-time Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Education and Professional Studies - EDN Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Griffith University is seeking a dynamic and strategically minded Research Support Officer to play a pivotal role in advancing research excellence across the School of Education and Professional Studies and the Griffith Institute for Educational Research (GIER). Working closely with the Head and Dean, Education and Professional Studies, research leaders and key stakeholders, you will drive initiatives that strengthen research performance, foster a vibrant research culture, and build research capacity across the School and Institute. This influential role offers the opportunity to lead research development projects, support the growth of collaborative research groups and strategic partnerships, and enhance the visibility, impact and engagement of world-class research. If you are passionate about enabling research success, translating strategy into action, and supporting researchers to maximise their impact, this is an exciting opportunity to contribute to transformative research initiatives that make a difference in education and society. Key responsibilities include but not limited to: Lead research development initiatives by coordinating research groups, capacity-building programs and strategic projects that strengthen research performance and culture across the School and GIER. Provide expert research support and advice to senior leaders, researchers and committees on research priorities, opportunities, governance and strategic initiatives. Drive research funding success through the coordination of grant development activities, funding opportunities and collaborative research partnerships. Enhance research visibility and impact by implementing communication, engagement and knowledge translation activities that promote the profile and influence of School and GIER research. Deliver research performance insights and governance support through data analysis, reporting, stakeholder engagement and the coordination of research planning and decision-making processes. About you The successful candidate will have a relevant postgraduate qualification and/or substantial experience in research development, research management, higher education administration or a related field. You will also have: Demonstrated experience leading and coordinating research development initiatives, strategic projects, research groups or capacity-building programs, with the ability to deliver outcomes in complex organisational environments. Proven ability to support research funding activities, facilitate collaboration, and build productive relationships with researchers, industry, government, community and other external stakeholders. Highly developed written and verbal communication skills, with experience developing and implementing strategies that enhance research visibility, engagement, reputation and impact across diverse audiences. Demonstrated ability to analyse complex data and information, prepare high-quality reports and briefing materials, and provide evidence-based advice to support strategic planning, governance and decision-making. Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to work collaboratively, influence outcomes and build effective partnerships across a broad range of stakeholders. Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, coordinate multiple initiatives, and identify opportunities for process and service improvement. Desirable: Experience working within a university, research institute or knowledge-intensive environment. Knowledge of the Australian higher education and research funding landscape, including competitive grant schemes, research impact and engagement frameworks. What we can offer This is a fixed term (available until 31 December 2026), full-time position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast (preferred) or Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time base salary for a HEW Level 7 is in the range $104,504 - $113,219 per annum, plus 17% employer superannuation. The total FTE package is in the range $122,270 - $132,466 per annum. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About you section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights.  Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Debbie Heck, Head and Dean, School of Education and Professional Studies at d.heck@griffith.edu.au . For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Theresa Burke, Talent Acquisition Partner on t.burke@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Tuesday, 15 September 2026 at 11.59pm. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Research Fellow Southport, Australia PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia Nathan, Australia Consultant Opportunity: Regional Marketing Manager (Greater China) Beijing, China Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Research Support Officer Parklands Dr, Southport QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
