    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148138149": {
      "title": "Griffith University Librarian (Client Experience)",
      "description": "Griffith University Librarian (Client Experience) | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Librarian (Client Experience) Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Library Campus Services - ILN Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Griffith University Library operates five campus libraries across four campus locations and provides services and expertise to the Griffith University teaching, learning and research community. The Library Campus Services team works closely with clients and establishes and maintains strong relationships to deliver useful and timely products and services, and access to resources. The Librarian (Client Experience) plays a key role in supporting both online and on-campus interactions, providing expert guidance to library staff and clients. Working collaboratively with two other librarians, the position supports Library Campus Services staff in the delivery of information services and contributes to the continuous improvement of user-focused services. The role works closely with the Coordinator and Library Campus Services Supervisors to ensure responsive, high-quality services that meet the evolving needs of the Griffith community. Key Responsibilities Deliver support for clients and library staff in accessing and using a range of library resources and services including first-tier referrals to services provided within Griffith University. Identify, develop and provide training to Library Campus Services staff in the delivery of information services and resources for complex client enquiries. Contribute to user-centric services in the development, implementation and review of services and systems by analysing and evaluating data. Proactively contribute to the development and documentation of policies, standards, protocols and procedures for delivery of quality services. Apply professional knowledge to present solutions which improve library services. Provide support and collaborate with other areas of the library to deliver small projects to enhance the client experience. Assist in the development and organising of engagement activities. Undertake regular personal and professional development to enhance knowledge and skills to enable a high level of service in a continuously changing environment. About you Degree in Library and Information Science with the ability to demonstrate relevant experience or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education/training which would allow professional membership of the Australian Library and Information Association (ALIA). Excellent communication skills with demonstrated ability to engage and collaborate with professional and academic staff and students. What we can offer This is continuing opportunity and is based at Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Base Salary HEW 5 in the range of $82,415 - $92,456 per annum plus 17% Superannuation. The salary including superannuation is in the range $96,426 -$108,174 per annum. Additional Information As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role, please refer to the qualifications above and the position description . (If applying through the Indeed jobs platform, please include your cover letter as the first page of your resume). Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For further information relating to the position, please contact Michelle Postlethwaite, Coordinator Library Campus Services m.postlethwaite@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Tuesday 22nd September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. Candidates must have Australian work rights and may be subject to a National criminal history check. Sponsorship is not offered for this position. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Service Centre Support Officer Nathan, Australia Senior Commercial Research Officer Southport, Australia Senior Commercial Research Officer Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. × Continue Librarian (Client Experience) University Dr, Southport QLD 4215, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000148116409": {
      "title": "Operations Coordinator (Open Space)",
      "description": "Griffith University Operations Coordinator (Open Space) | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Operations Coordinator (Open Space) Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Campus Life Facilities North - ONA Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity The Operations Coordinator – Open Space will support coordinated delivery of Landscape/Open Space operations, with a focus on Northern campuses maintenance coordination and ESP/Hardscape program delivery support across the University. The role will work closely with the Operations Lead – Open Space, internal teams, contractors and campus/project stakeholders to maintain service continuity and support agreed program outcomes. The position will primarily support Northern campuses, with coordination support to Gold Coast as required. Key responsibilities Coordinate BAU Landscape/Open Space activities across the Northern campuses, including gardens, lawns, sports fields, irrigation, trees, bushland interfaces, campus presentation and reactive works Support agreed ESP and Hardscape program delivery across the University through contractor scheduling, site coordination, field verification, work follow-up and progress reporting Coordinate landscape contractors, subcontractors and internal team activities to achieve safe, efficient and quality service outcomes Assist with scoping, planning and sequencing of landscape, biodiversity, hardscape and open space improvement works under the direction of the Operations Lead – Open Space Infrastructure Monitor work quality, campus presentation, defects, risks, WHS matters and contractor performance, escalating issues where required Support tree management, weed management, fire trail maintenance, HRB preparation, storm/weather response and other operational programs within the open space portfolio Assist with procurement inputs, quotes, work orders, contractor documentation, service request follow-up and budget/work tracking as required Use University systems and digital tools to support work coordination, reporting, field records, photos, service requests and asset information updates Liaise with Facilities, Minor Projects, Capital Works, Engineering, contractors and other stakeholders to coordinate external area works and minimise operational disruption Support consistent service delivery standards across campuses, including coordination support at Gold Coast or other campuses when required Work collaboratively with the Operations Lead – Open Space Infrastructure, Open Space Officer, Gold Coast Coordinator and relevant teams to align BAU priorities, ESP/Hardscape delivery, contractor performance and reporting requirements. About you Practical experience in landscape operations, parks and gardens, horticulture, sports turf, natural area management, civil/hardscape maintenance or similar open space environments Strong contractor coordination, field follow-up and service delivery skills Ability to balance daily BAU operational priorities with project/program delivery requirements Sound judgement in identifying risks, defects, presentation issues, WHS matters and service gaps Confidence using, or quickly learning, digital systems for work orders, service requests, photos, reporting and asset information Strong communication skills and ability to work with contractors, internal teams, Facilities, project teams and campus stakeholders Ability to work across multiple campuses and adapt to changing operational priorities A practical, organised and solutions-focused approach to maintaining safe, functional and well-presented campus open spaces. Diploma, Advanced Certificate or equivalent experience in horticulture, landscape construction, parks and gardens, sports turf, natural area management or a related discipline. Demonstrated experience in coordinating landscape, open space, natural area or similar operational works within a multi-site or complex service environment. Sound understanding of WHS requirements, environmental obligations, plant and machinery use, contractor interface and practical site-based problem solving. Current Class C driver licence, with the ability to use or quickly learn relevant University systems and mobile/digital tools. What we can offer This is a full-time, fixed term opportunity for 6 months primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 6 – Base - $94,966.18 - $101,295.51 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $111,110.42 - $118,515.75. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information, please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role; please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For further specifics about the role, please reach out to Dr Vatsal Naik, Operations Lead - Open Space, on [email protected] . For application and recruitment advice, please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner, on [email protected] Closing date: Open until filled. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
