    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000147831529": {
      "title": "Griffith University Commercialisation Manager (Medtech)",
      "description": "Griffith University Commercialisation Manager (Medtech) | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Commercialisation Manager (Medtech) Full-time Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Griffith Enterprise - CMU Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Exciting opportunity to join a dynamic commercialisation team to lead and drive commercialisation and commercial partnerships for world leading research in the Medtech area. Playing a pivotal role in supporting Griffith's ambitions is Griffith Enterprise , the university’s dedicated commercialisation office, managing and commercialising the universities intellectual property and research expertise. Griffith Enterprise’s mission is to manage and facilitate the commercialisation of intellectual property and research excellence from Griffith University researchers via the most appropriate commercialisation pathway, ensuring optimum outcomes for all of our partners whilst protecting and enhancing the reputation of the university. By translating and commercialising ground-breaking technologies and research excellence, empowering a culture of collaboration, and prioritising our partner’s needs we help them achieve their strategic ambitions and generate global impact. Job Description As the Manager, Commercialisation (Medtech) you will be responsible for identifying, developing and leading commercialisation opportunities, partnerships, transactions and strategic initiatives in the Medtech area as part of the Life Science team focussing on commercialisation of technologies such as medical devices and digital health. You will work closely with Griffith researchers to identify and assess potential new intellectual property and through business development activities negotiate commercialisation transactions such as licences, start-ups, research agreements to take the research to the market. This will include researchers across all of Griffith’s campuses including the Australian Centre for Precision Health and Technology at Griffith. You will play a key role in advancing commercialisation awareness and skills across the University and, along with key Griffith staff, engaging with partners to help shape strategic partnerships.  As a senior member of the team, you will lead all aspects of the commercialisation and IP management process, from early-stage research to the negotiations of deals and establishing start-up companies. About you To be successful in this role you will hold a postgraduate degree and 5+ years’ experience in a similar role and a strong track record of success in identifying, managing and commercialising intellectual property in the field of Medtech based research through licences, research collaborations and/or start-ups. You will also have technical knowledge in a relevant area of Medtech/digital health and demonstrated business development expertise and a track record will be required. Your ability to deal with complex situations and communicate clearly will be an asset to the team. Demonstrated skills required to assess early-stage technologies and understand intellectual property (IP) management and protection, including patents and other forms of IP; identify and negotiate commercial opportunities; and a proven ability to scope, pitch and negotiate commercialisation transactions are essential. You will need to be a self-starter and team player. You will be given the autonomy, responsibility and required support to make a significant contribution to Griffith Enterprise and the University. What we can offer This is a continuing, full-time position and will be primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations.  Griffith provides access to fleet cars if needed to travel between its locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range A competitive remuneration package will be negotiated with the successful applicant. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About you section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details A non-confidential deal sheet highlighting your relevant deal track record Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact griffithenterprise@griffth.edu.au . For application support, please contact People Services on (07) 373 54011 and quote reference number REF11027P . Closing date: Tuesday, 22 September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Understanding and addressing anti-government and sovereign citizen extremism in Australia Nathan, Australia PhD Scholarship: Foundation Models for Anomaly Detection Nathan, Australia Senior Commercial Research Officer Southport, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Commercialisation Manager (Medtech) Parklands Dr, Southport QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
