    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000147408699": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer",
      "description": "Griffith University Associate Lecturer - Chemistry | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Associate Lecturer - Chemistry Part-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Part Time Department ID: School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences - PAM Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description The School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences is home to world-class researchers and teachers dedicated to advancing human health through discovery and innovation. Our programs integrate biomedical, pharmaceutical, and clinical sciences to equip graduates with the skills to transform healthcare practice.   The School is also leading the integration of digital health across all programs, driving innovation in health education and research. As an Associate Lecturer (Level A) - Chemistry, you will contribute to the School’s teaching excellence and research impact. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Lead and support undergraduate chemistry workshops and laboratory classes, particularly in organic chemistry and analytical chemistry, ensuring activities are delivered safely, effectively and in alignment with course requirements. Conduct lectures when required, under the guidance of the course convenor or relevant academic lead, and contribute to continuity of teaching across assigned chemistry courses. Prepare, facilitate and review practical and workshop teaching materials in consultation with course convenors, technical staff and relevant academic supervisors. Support high quality learning and teaching outcomes for students through active, student-centred and technology-enhanced teaching approaches, including problem-oriented and authentic learning activities in chemistry. This is a part-time (0.60 FTE), fixed-term appointment until 2 March 2029 based at Griffith University’s Gold Coast location. As Griffith University is a multi-campus institution you may be required to work at other campuses or other sites on occasion. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level A range $82,704 - $111,219 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $96,764 - $130,126 per annum. Qualifications What matters most is your drive to create a brighter future that benefits all. Through our core principles of excellence, ethics and engagement, you’ll thrive on seeing the direct and lasting impact you’ll have on every community and every future. You will also have: Hold a degree in chemistry or a closely related discipline, with demonstrated knowledge and capability in organic chemistry and analytical chemistry. Prior experience supporting or delivering chemistry teaching in a higher education setting, including workshops, laboratory classes and technology-enhanced learning, is desirable. Commitment to integrating technology-enhanced and student-centred learning approaches. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to foster positive, collaborative relationships. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the Position Description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Jennifer Boddy, Head of School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences at [email protected] . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] . Closing date: Monday, 21 September 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000149454639": {
      "title": "Griffith University Senior Analyst, Transformation",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Analyst, Transformation | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Senior Analyst, Transformation Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Transformation - TMO Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the Opportunity The Senior Analyst will work together with Executive sponsors, senior leaders, and the Transformation team to deliver important strategic projects. This position is accountable for analysis of data and information, with a view to understanding the current state and identifying pain points and improvement opportunities. The occupant will engage stakeholders at various levels of the University to build solutions to improve or transform ways of working. This position will solve complex challenges through insightful data analysis and effective stakeholder engagement. The position will be involved in important strategic discussions on Griffith’s future direction and how Griffith can achieve the ambitions in our new strategic plan. Key Responsibilities Lead workshops for large groups of stakeholders including end users and senior management teams eliciting solutions and future vision. Assess, analyse and research data and information, policies and objectives. Recommend opportunities for improvement that are aligned to the University’s strategic goals and compatible with its complex organisational structures. Secure agreement from senior stakeholders on recommended solution options. Conduct complex data analytics to assess the current state and forecast the impact of the future options. Prepare insightful and persuasive documents which detail the insights from data analysis. Lead sprint teams, including business analysts and subject matter experts in analysis and delivery phases. Mentor and support operational teams in embracing a culture of continuous improvement and in understanding and managing process change. Provide advice to operational and project teams on impacts of proposed changes on related systems, processes and organisational structures, as well as considering impacts on other areas of the University’s operations. Develop performance reporting for change activities, including assessment of costs, benefits and risks, preparation of specifications and reporting. Implement agreed solutions in collaboration with functional teams, key stakeholders, users and project teams, ensuring design, planning and testing components are delivered in alignment with the University’s project and change management framework. Support the Delivery Lead and Functional Lead in delivering on the objectives of the Program and the University Strategy, including immediate improvement priorities, as well as medium to long term transformation opportunities. Reinforce the spirit and goals of the transformation agenda and drive a culture of continuous improvement. Support compliance with relevant legislation and University policies and procedures, including equity and health & safety and exhibit good practice in relation to same. About you The occupant of this position will hold tertiary qualifications and extensive relevant experience in strategic analysis, data analysis and/or change projects; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. You will have strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work through complex issues and develop clear evidence-based recommendations. You will be a confident communicator and comfortable working with senior stakeholders. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and may be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time continuing opportunity based at the Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 9 – Base range - $137,165.65 - $142,070.17 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $160,483.80 - $166,222.09. Additional Information What we can offer This is a full time continuing opportunity based at the Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 9 – Base range - $137,165.65 - $142,070.17 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $160,483.80 - $166,222.09. Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Tuesday 29th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Salesforce Opportunities Nathan, Australia Dental Assistant Warwick, Australia Research Fellow Southport, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. × Continue Senior Analyst, Transformation 170 Kessels Road, Nathan, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000149772199": {
      "title": "Griffith University Talent Acquisition Consultant",
      "description": "Griffith University Talent Acquisition Consultant | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Talent Acquisition Consultant Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Talent Acquisition - HTA Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the Opportunity As a Talent Acquisition Consultant, you will play a key role in supporting the delivery of talent acquisition services across the University. Working closely with the Talent Acquisition team, including central portfolios and academic groups, you will assist with a wide range of recruitment and talent-related activities to ensure a seamless hiring experience. Reporting to the Talent Acquisition Coordinator, you will provide administrative and operational support across the end-to-end recruitment process, while also offering guidance on relevant policies, procedures, and talent practices. You will collaborate with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders, building strong relationships and delivering responsive, customer-focused support to attract and secure top talent. Key Responsibilities Support the delivery of key Talent Acquisition processes and systems, including the administration and processing of paid appointments and recruitment activities. Coordinate interview logistics, ensuring a seamless candidate and stakeholder experience through the organisation of venues, catering, parking, schedules, and related arrangements. Prepare and process employment offers and associated recruitment documentation, ensuring accuracy and timely completion. Compile, prepare, and coordinate recruitment materials and documentation, including interview packs, selection reports, and other relevant paperwork to be able to send to staff file. Assist in the development of engaging recruitment marketing materials, including LinkedIn content and talent attraction collateral, in partnership with Talent Acquisition Partners. Manage financial administration activities, including raising purchase orders, processing invoices, reconciling transactions, and maintaining accurate records in collaboration with Finance and other stakeholders. Build and maintain strong professional relationships with internal and external stakeholders, fostering effective communication and collaboration across the University. Maintain and update employee and position data within PeopleSoft, ensuring compliance with position management processes, data integrity requirements, and HR governance protocols. Work both independently and collaboratively as part of a high-performing Talent Acquisition team, effectively managing priorities and delivering outcomes within agreed timeframes. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant tertiary qualifications in Human Resources, Business Administration, Safety, or a relevant field, or possess relevant work experience in Human Resources and Safety. Strong attention to detail, with the ability to consistently produce accurate, high-quality work while managing competing priorities and meeting deadlines. Candidates must have full, unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full-time continuing opportunity based at the either the Gold Coast or Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 5 – Base range - $82,415.66 - $92,456.55 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $96,426.31 - $108,174.16. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Open until filled. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Payroll and Benefits Officer Nathan, Australia Lecturer (Level B) in Midwifery Meadowbrook, Australia Senior Analyst, Transformation Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Talent Acquisition Consultant 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
