    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000149771789": {
      "title": "Griffith University Payroll and Benefits Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Payroll and Benefits Officer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Payroll and Benefits Officer Contract Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: People Services - HSY Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the Opportunity The Payroll and Benefits Officer is a key contributor to the delivery of accurate, compliant, and customer-focused payroll services within a large and complex higher education environment. This role is responsible for the efficient administration and processing of a broad range of payroll and employment-related activities, ensuring employees are paid accurately and on time while meeting all legislative, taxation, and University compliance requirements. As a valued member of a high-performing Payroll team, the Payroll and Benefits Officer provides specialist advice and support to employees, managers, and other stakeholders across all stages of the employee lifecycle. The role supports effective payroll governance, risk management, data integrity, and continuous improvement initiatives, contributing to operational excellence and a positive employee experience. Success in this position requires extensive payroll expertise, strong analytical and problem-solving skills, sound judgment, and a commitment to delivering exceptional service within a complex industrial relations and regulatory framework. Key Responsibilities Deliver accurate and timely payroll services across the employee lifecycle, including employee changes, leave, superannuation, salary packaging and terminations. Maintain payroll and HR records, ensuring data accuracy, compliance and integrity. Provide responsive payroll advice and support to employees, managers and stakeholders. Identify and resolve payroll discrepancies, compliance issues and system-related queries. Support payroll reconciliations, audits, system improvements and continuous improvement initiatives. Build strong working relationships across HR, Finance and the broader University community. Contribute to a collaborative, high-performing team culture while maintaining current knowledge of payroll legislation, compliance requirements and best practice. About you Relevant tertiary qualifications in Business, Human Resources, Payroll Administration or a related discipline, and/or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education. Demonstrated experience in payroll administration within a large and complex organisation and experience interpreting industrial instruments, employment legislation and payroll-related taxation and superannuation requirements. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is full-time opportunity based at Brisbane South (Nathan).  As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. HEW 5 Salary – Base range - $82,415.65 - $92,456.55 + 17% super. Full package range - $96,426 - $108,147. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing Date: Wednesday 30th September at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Talent Acquisition Consultant Nathan, Australia Lecturer (Level B) in Midwifery Meadowbrook, Australia Senior Analyst, Transformation Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Payroll and Benefits Officer 170 Kessels Road, Nathan, Australia Contract I'm interested I'm interested"
