    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000150280479": {
      "title": "Griffith University Scientific Officer Laboratory and Preclinical Experience",
      "description": "Griffith University Scientific Officer Laboratory and Preclinical Experience | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Scientific Officer Laboratory and Preclinical Experience Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Health - HLS Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description We’re looking for a passionate and highly organised Scientific Officer to join our Technical Partners Health team, supporting teaching and learning across the School of Medicine, Dentistry and Paramedicine and the School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences . In this hands-on role, you’ll provide technical and scientific support for practical teaching and learning, working closely with academic staff and technical teams to deliver high-quality, safe, and innovative learning experiences for students. You’ll thrive in a collaborative, supportive and respectful environment where continuous improvement, adaptability and teamwork are highly valued, and where your expertise will directly contribute to outstanding student outcomes. As a Scientific Officer, you will: Prepare, set up and maintain laboratory spaces across different facilities, ensuring practical teaching sessions run smoothly and safely while supporting different technical teams Collaborate with technical and academic staff and course convenors to develop and deliver best-practice practical teaching activities and procedures Manage equipment and consumables, including stocktakes, procurement, maintenance and calibration to industry standards Develop and maintain documentation such as lab resource statements, risk assessments and standard operating procedures Provide technical instruction and support to staff, while contributing to special events, workshops and continuous improvement initiatives About you To be successful in this role, you will: Hold a relevant health or science-based degree or have an equivalent combination of training, knowledge, and experience in a similar technical support environment Have demonstrated experience supporting clinical, preclinical, simulation, or laboratory-based teaching activities Possess strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks, prioritise effectively and adapt to changing demands Demonstrate excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with academic staff and technical teams Show a commitment to continuous improvement, with a proactive, detail-oriented approach and a focus on delivering high-quality, safe and inclusive learning environments What we can offer This is a continuing, full-time position primarily based at the Griffith University’s Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time base salary for a HEW Level 5 is in the range $82,415 - $92,456 per annum, plus 17% employer superannuation. The total FTE package is in the range $96,426- $108,174 per annum. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Opportunities for internal mobility Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Dr Lirio Calderon-Gomez, Technical Manager for the Laboratory and Practical Experience Technical Partners Health team at l.calderon-gomez@griffith.edu.au . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au Closing date: 11th October 2026, 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Scientific Assistant (Biosciences) Nathan, Australia Research Fellow Southport, Australia Lecturer (Level B) Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. × Continue Scientific Officer Laboratory and Preclinical Experience 1 Parklands Dr, Southport QLD 4215, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000150272830": {
      "title": "Griffith University Administration Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Administration Officer – Marketing and Communications | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Administration Officer – Marketing and Communications Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Marketing and Communications - OER Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the Opportunity The Schools Engagement and Pathways Administration Officer supports the Senior Future Students Manager and the Future Students team more broadly. Under general direction, this position is responsible for providing high-quality administrative and operational support for the team’s school engagement activities, student ambassador program, campus visits, events and associated business processes. Key responsibilities Coordinate the end-to-end administration of student ambassador engagements, including recruitment and engagement activities, onboarding requirements, access arrangements and maintenance of casual student ambassador profiles. Coordinate administrative and logistical support for school engagement activities, including but not limited to; campus visits, tours, presentations, room bookings, catering and transport. Monitor designated individual and shared email accounts, triage enquiries and provide timely, professional support to student ambassadors, school contacts and internal stakeholders. Provide administrative support, including records management, and process improvement. Support projects through research, data collection, and the preparation of reports, presentations, correspondence, and submissions. Maintain databases and online systems, process procurement and financial transactions, and assist with system improvements. Apply policies and procedures and contribute to the development of administrative processes. Monitor budgets, maintain financial records, and prepare invoicing, costings and reports. Build effective relationships with internal and external stakeholders. About you The occupant of this position will hold a minimum of an associate diploma qualification and at least two years relevant work experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant skills, knowledge and experience. In addition, you will demonstrate: Experience providing administrative and operational support within a complex, service-focused environment. Strong organisational and time-management skills, including the ability to coordinate multiple activities, manage changing priorities and meet operational deadlines. Demonstrated attention to detail and experience maintaining accurate information across databases, spreadsheets and online systems. Candidates must have full unrestricted Australian work rights and will be subject to a National criminal history check. What we can offer This is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 12 months primarily based at our Gold Coast campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 5 - $82,415.66 - $92,456.55 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $96,426.31 - $108,174.16. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 4th October at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Talent Acquisition Consultant Nathan, Australia Payroll and Benefits Officer Nathan, Australia Project Coordinator (Cyber Security) Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Administration Officer – Marketing and Communications Parklands Dr, Southport QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    }
